{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:35:09.802Z","ordinal":9494,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035a3-086c-7020-a149-5e66cf01e9bf","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cb90c64b487d0b5498b5d5a3a0370","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe approved spec now treats local activation as capability evidence, not a boolean copied from repository content. That is the key security boundary enabling always-installed hooks without letting a fresh clone silently activate execution or egress.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nThe independent reviewer approved the final spec with no remaining issues. I’m running the repository-required full pre-commit check now; after it passes I’ll commit the design document and hand it back for your review before implementation planning."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787607308413,"completed_at_ms":1787607309802}}
