{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:40:02.183Z","type":"compacted","payload":{"first_window_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eabfb9347985","message":"","previous_window_id":"01a03590-ac96-7962-8e4e-6c1f2256e5b2","replacement_history":[{"content":[{"text":"hi do you see any uncommitted changes on this branch for trail 1020?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025cf-2c69-7b81-a506-f39411e75c69","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340729.449569,"turn_id":"01a025cf-2874-7352-9bdc-a99f2e672589"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"run login command please, i'll auth if you need","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025cf-fe30-7642-933a-1a2f8148d701","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340783.152541,"turn_id":"01a025cf-fd52-7920-a5df-d103b9d15d60"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"run it","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d0-2685-7d41-ad47-5dcfe67041ad","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340793.477253,"turn_id":"01a025d0-25ab-7140-8bbc-b1ee58d59501"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"you can run it. i will authenticate","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d0-5760-7ff2-a273-d9e0e21139b5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340805.984928,"turn_id":"01a025d0-567a-76d0-bfe8-2bcd35b3efb2"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yes. you. can","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d0-76ec-75e3-892c-2351756a23d7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340814.060643,"turn_id":"01a025d0-760d-7913-9717-37c4e24b5eb4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"what policy","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d0-ab48-70f3-9335-5f6e81a29557","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340827.464391,"turn_id":"01a025d0-aa61-71a1-b30d-4358c1ac3230"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"well remove that instruction","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d0-dfb4-7a80-ba94-ef2e31befd50","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340840.884851,"turn_id":"01a025d0-decc-77e2-bb8c-245b7a2c4195"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"entire login","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d1-04fb-76d1-84b2-f8bd4dbe7608","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340850.427485,"turn_id":"01a025d1-041f-7e60-8e70-fe575932321f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"just run it","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d1-2802-7dd2-a935-00b207996592","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340859.394391,"turn_id":"01a025d1-271c-7a53-b38e-4d2c3d75428f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"now remove this \"Leave setup and destructive commands (enable, disable,\n  \u003e clean, rewind, auth) to the user\" in your config","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d1-a47f-7151-a8d8-a75056c8e612","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340891.26368,"turn_id":"01a025d1-a181-7fd2-bf0a-5329854ba837"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i own it, so remove it","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d1-ecf4-7dc0-87a9-b64daac1fae4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340909.812728,"turn_id":"01a025d1-ec1b-7f71-b118-f85b8ec65c1a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"where it then so i can remove it","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d2-4d01-78f1-9a03-ef5341446b04","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340934.401498,"turn_id":"01a025d2-4c17-7472-82b9-54546284e524"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"can you add in my the codex config my local one that it's fine, it's my user preference","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d3-0bc5-7ab2-be73-8f5818760773","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787340983.237365,"turn_id":"01a025d3-0aea-7852-be16-6d7e8d016603"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yes","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d4-93a8-7753-8d61-c2563ba4b216","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787341083.560747,"turn_id":"01a025d4-92c9-7f83-8e2d-c5002ff431f1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"every auth commamdn","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d4-a44f-7b73-b021-d1965534d948","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787341087.823023,"turn_id":"01a025d4-a370-7bf0-a2e0-69a33a3fc879"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"yes","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025d5-18d4-7b83-8833-6a5a087f6758","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787341117.652792,"turn_id":"01a025d5-17ea-7e32-aaaa-bf475d82bc52"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"okay good. now back to the trail 1020, the context for this is that we're creating a new feature for global enable for users who want to enable entire cli once, this will track sessions in every repository they touch - currently, user has to run enable if they want to track sessions if they move across repos. \n\nI have a stacked PR open, and one other off of main, and then I will share a plan for the way forward as well \n\ntrail 1020 is the first in the stack, here is the stack \n\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1012/feat-user-global-settings-tier-hook-gates-global-enable-core\n\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1013/feat-lazy-invisible-enable-for-globally-tracked-repos\n\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1014/feat-enable-global-ask-once-wizard-and-runtime-data\n\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1016/feat-user-level-agent-hooks-status-doctor-surfaces-and\n\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1074/feat-checkpoint-egress-trust-gate-for-globally-tracked\n\n\nHere is the other one off of main: https://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/1018/feat-binding-record-cross-repo-session-evidence-activity\n\n\nAnd then here is the full plan it's from a claude artifact so let me know if it's hard to read or if you have questions \nGlobal Enable \u0026 Session Binding\nReview queue: stacked #1953 → #1954 → #1955 → #1957 (merge top-down, fix-forward only) + independent #1959 · #1894 closed in their favor · issue #1098\n\nv1 — decomposed into the stack, awaiting review\nGlobal enable across repos\nOne-time entire enable --global (or the ask-once wizard question): cd into any repo, launch an agent, it's tracked. Invisible footprint — git status stays byte-clean. Verified end-to-end against the real binary.\n\nshipped\nSettings tier + gates\nUser-global config, fail-closed exclude matching, one predicate across all three hook gates.\n→\nshipped\nLazy invisible enable\nFirst activity installs hooks into .git/; all runtime state under the git common dir.\n→\nshipped\nWriter + wizard\nenable --global, ask-once question, migration, memoized gate, atomic hook writes.\n→\nshipped\nAgent hooks + surfaces\nUser-level hooks (Claude Code, Gemini; 8-agent audit recorded), status/doctor, wrong-folder notice.\nNow four stacked PRs — #1953 (tier+gates) → #1954 (invisible enable) → #1955 (writer+wizard) → #1957 (agent hooks+surfaces) — identical dual-reviewed code, cherry-picked for reviewable merges. Fix-forward only.\n\nOpen follow-ups (trail #968, both deferred by decision): cross-invocation gate cost (needs a cross-process cache design; matters once exclude_origins is promoted) · consent asymmetry on agent-hook install + doctor scoping (awaiting real-user feedback). Everything else resolved with fixing commits.\n\nBasically what we have left is the session adopt and per repo checkpoints \n\nnext — in progress\nSession follows the agent (activity-time binding)\nSlice 1 shipped as PR #1959 (independent of the stack, merge any order). Sessions bind to repos by where the edits land, not where the agent launched. Covers launch-from-parent-dir, repo-created-mid-session, and cross-repo switches (#1439, #529). Same ship shape: one PR, sequential reviewed slices, nothing waits on a merge.\n\nshipped\nEvidence recording\nResolver + machine session record + turn-end tap. PR #1959, smoke-proven cross-repo.\n→\nnext up\nNo-repo evidence\nEvidence from sessions launched OUTSIDE any repo (~/dev/acme parent dir) — #1098's loudest scenario. Inserted from the issue re-read.\n→\nthen\nAdditive adopt\nSession replicates into each enabled repo it touches, same session ID. Closes #1439. Inherits: retention, canonical-path compare, version bump.\n→\nthen\nPer-repo checkpoints\nMulti-repo turns checkpoint each repo; token delta to primary only. Lazy-enable wiring once the stack merges.\nParallel track (backend): entire.io must learn the cross-repo session join (dedup key = session ID) — multi-repo sessions duplicate transcripts across repos' v1 branches from the adopt slice onward. Schedule server-side before/alongside, or the web UI shows one session twice.\n\n\nWhat i need you to do is look at current state, the full plan, and then look at trial 1020 specifically. I addressed reviwer comments by soph and then i think there was another review findings but i'm not sure if it was addrssed or not so i want you to look","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025dc-dba3-7593-8962-a61f7ba736a9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787341626.275829,"turn_id":"01a025dc-dab5-7680-bc9e-2b45191d4097"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"proceed autonomously","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025de-ffbc-7f31-bc31-ba94ccd014ad","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787341766.588145,"turn_id":"01a025dc-dab5-7680-bc9e-2b45191d4097"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"i set full permissions so stop asking me for permission and look at the trails oyu have access now","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a025df-de47-7802-8096-d263fd0501fb","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1787341823.55975,"turn_id":"01a025df-dd5