{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:46:05.746Z","ordinal":9660,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbb953cd087d08b2f10d65d1700b0","status":"completed","call_id":"call_lrSoFUeyEDgiFYCF5b0WWRBR","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\\n@@\\n-**Status:** Approved for implementation planning  \\n+**Status:** Revised after product-behavior clarification; awaiting approval  \\n@@\\n-- all global tracking configuration is edited only in the user's\\n+- global activation and exclusion policy are edited in the user's\\n   `~/.config/entire/settings.json` (or the path selected by\\n   `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`);\\n-- the CLI does not provide commands or wizard flows that mutate the `global`\\n-  settings block;\\n+- the CLI does not provide commands or wizard flows that turn global tracking\\n+  on or off;\\n+- the existing pre-push trust prompt, `entire trust`/`--revoke`, and\\n+  settings-backed egress gate remain product behavior;\\n - supported user-level agent hooks are ordinary installed infrastructure and are\\n-  inert until repository policy activates them; and\\n+  inert until repository policy activates them, without changing Claude Code\\n+  or Gemini CLI event coverage; and\\n@@\\n-- Make the user settings file the sole write surface for global activation,\\n-  exclusions, and trust.\\n+- Make the user settings file the sole direct configuration surface for global\\n+  activation and exclusions while preserving the existing trust UX and its\\n+  settings-backed consent writes.\\n@@\\n - Preserve existing explicitly enabled repositories and linked-worktree\\n   isolation.\\n+- Preserve the current pre-push trust choices, egress hold/drain behavior, and\\n+  Claude Code/Gemini CLI lifecycle coverage.\\n@@\\n-- A global-enablement or trust wizard.\\n+- A global-enablement wizard.\\n+- Redesigning the pre-push trust experience, `entire trust`, checkpoint egress,\\n+  or the supported Claude Code/Gemini CLI event surfaces.\\n@@\\n-### Global settings are file-only\\n+### Global activation is file-only\\n@@\\n-The refactor removes every CLI mutation path for this block:\\n+The refactor removes the CLI mutation paths for global activation:\\n \\n - `entire enable --global`;\\n - `entire disable --global`;\\n-- the ask-once global-tracking wizard question;\\n-- `entire trust` and `entire trust --revoke`; and\\n-- the interactive pre-push trust prompt, including the \\\"Always\\\" writer.\\n+- the ask-once global-tracking wizard question.\\n \\n-Status, doctor, and hold messages may show the resolved settings path and the\\n-specific keys a user needs to edit. They must not mutate the global block.\\n+`entire trust`, `entire trust --revoke`, and the interactive pre-push choices\\n+remain. They may update only egress-consent fields (`trust_all`,\\n+`trusted_origins`, and `trusted_paths`) in the same user settings file; they do\\n+not enable global tracking or change exclusions. Status and doctor continue to\\n+report both activation and trust state.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","create_time":1787607956.161815}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:46:05.861Z","ordinal":9661,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-3410ed0a-e582-46bd-890b-6a38bb6bf786","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -2,3 +2,3 @@\n \n-**Status:** Approved for implementation planning  \n+**Status:** Revised after product-behavior clarification; awaiting approval  \n **Date:** 2026-08-24  \n@@ -25,9 +25,12 @@\n \n-- all global tracking configuration is edited only in the user's\n+- global activation and exclusion policy are edited in the user's\n   `~/.config/entire/settings.json` (or the path selected by\n   `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`);\n-- the CLI does not provide commands or wizard flows that mutate the `global`\n-  settings block;\n+- the CLI does not provide commands or wizard flows that turn global tracking\n+  on or off;\n+- the existing pre-push trust prompt, `entire trust`/`--revoke`, and\n+  settings-backed egress gate remain product behavior;\n - supported user-level agent hooks are ordinary installed infrastructure and are\n-  inert until repository policy activates them; and\n+  inert until repository policy activates them, without changing Claude Code\n+  or Gemini CLI event coverage; and\n - existing repository-level `entire enable` behavior remains supported.\n@@ -40,4 +43,5 @@\n \n-- Make the user settings file the sole write surface for global activation,\n-  exclusions, and trust.\n+- Make the user settings file the sole direct configuration surface for global\n+  activation and exclusions while preserving the existing trust UX and its\n+  settings-backed consent writes.\n - Preserve a byte-clean worktree for repositories activated only by global\n@@ -55,2 +59,4 @@\n   isolation.\n+- Preserve the current pre-push trust choices, egress hold/drain behavior, and\n+  Claude Code/Gemini CLI lifecycle coverage.\n - Resolve every current trail finding with a regression test or by removing the\n@@ -61,3 +67,5 @@\n - A CLI editor for global settings.\n-- A global-enablement or trust wizard.\n+- A global-enablement wizard.\n+- Redesigning the pre-push trust experience, `entire trust`, checkpoint egress,\n+  or the supported Claude Code/Gemini CLI event surfaces.\n - Supporting user-level hooks for agents without a verified user-scope config\n@@ -73,3 +81,3 @@\n \n-### Global settings are file-only\n+### Global activation is file-only\n \n@@ -91,3 +99,3 @@\n \n-The refactor removes every CLI mutation path for this block:\n+The refactor removes the CLI mutation paths for global activation:\n \n@@ -95,8 +103,9 @@\n - `entire disable --global`;\n-- the ask-once global-tracking wizard question;\n-- `entire trust` and `entire trust --revoke`; and\n-- the interactive pre-push trust prompt, including the \"Always\" writer.\n+- the ask-once global-tracking wizard question.\n \n-Status, doctor, and hold messages may show the resolved settings path and the\n-specific keys a user needs to edit. They must not mutate the global block.\n+`entire trust`, `entire trust --revoke`, and the interactive pre-push choices\n+remain. They may update only egress-consent fields (`trust_all`,\n+`trusted_origins`, and `trusted_paths`) in the same user settings file; they do\n+not enable global tracking or change exclusions. Status and doctor continue to\n+report both activation and trust state.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787607965793,"completed_at_ms":1787607965861}}
