{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:46:17.360Z","ordinal":9666,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbb9f3a9487d0b47e18527ed7cbf7","status":"completed","call_id":"call_OJnz4zQcU8M1QVHQg5vrPHXK","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\\n@@\\n-### File-defined consent\\n+### Settings-backed consent\\n@@\\n-Because the CLI no longer mutates trust entries, there is no asymmetric identity\\n-pruning or revoke operation. A stale origin entry remains explicit user\\n-configuration; removing that entry from the settings file is the revocation.\\n-Status reports the exact currently matched trust source.\\n+The existing consent surfaces remain:\\n+\\n+- `entire trust` grants trust for the current normalized repository identity;\\n+- `entire trust --revoke` withdraws trust previously granted for that\\n+  repository;\\n+- the interactive pre-push prompt offers \\\"Yes\\\", \\\"Not now\\\", and \\\"Always\\\"; and\\n+- users may edit the same trust fields directly in the settings file.\\n+\\n+All writers use one identity derivation and one atomic settings update. A small\\n+machine-local trust-grant ledger records which origin/path keys a CLI or\\n+pre-push grant wrote for each canonical worktree. Re-granting after an identity\\n+change removes superseded keys from that worktree's prior grant before writing\\n+the new identity; revoke removes both the current identity and every key in that\\n+record. Hand-authored entries not recorded as a grant are never heuristically\\n+deleted. This preserves origin-wide trust while fixing origin-to-path and\\n+path-to-origin stale grants. Status reports the exact currently matched trust\\n+source.\\n@@\\n-Pre-push never prompts. If an untrusted globally activated repository has no\\n-pending checkpoints, the hook emits nothing. If checkpoints are pending, the\\n-hook prints one single-line hold notice, returns success, and leaves the user's\\n-normal branch push untouched. The notice points to the resolved user settings\\n-file instead of an unavailable command.\\n+Pre-push preserves the current trust flow. If an untrusted globally activated\\n+repository has no pending checkpoints, the hook emits nothing and does not\\n+prompt. If checkpoints are pending and a real interactive terminal is\\n+available, the hook opens the three-choice trust prompt using `/dev/tty`, never\\n+Git's stdin:\\n+\\n+- \\\"Yes\\\" records the current repository identity and drains the queued\\n+  checkpoints after re-evaluating policy;\\n+- \\\"Not now\\\" keeps capturing locally and leaves the queue for a later push; and\\n+- \\\"Always\\\" records `trust_all`, re-evaluates policy, and drains the queue.\\n+\\n+If the prompt is unavailable, aborted, or fails—or if persistence or policy\\n+re-evaluation fails—the checkpoint queue remains held while the user's normal\\n+branch push continues. Accessible mode must use a supported explicit selection\\n+path or hold; it must never accept a default implicitly, panic, or consume\\n+pre-push stdin. The held message remains actionable and points to `entire trust`\\n+and the resolved settings file.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","create_time":1787607966.365392}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:46:17.465Z","ordinal":9667,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-ab781f7d-767c-49f0-a58b-62301bc43d23","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -349,3 +349,3 @@\n \n-### File-defined consent\n+### Settings-backed consent\n \n@@ -366,6 +366,19 @@\n \n-Because the CLI no longer mutates trust entries, there is no asymmetric identity\n-pruning or revoke operation. A stale origin entry remains explicit user\n-configuration; removing that entry from the settings file is the revocation.\n-Status reports the exact currently matched trust source.\n+The existing consent surfaces remain:\n+\n+- `entire trust` grants trust for the current normalized repository identity;\n+- `entire trust --revoke` withdraws trust previously granted for that\n+  repository;\n+- the interactive pre-push prompt offers \"Yes\", \"Not now\", and \"Always\"; and\n+- users may edit the same trust fields directly in the settings file.\n+\n+All writers use one identity derivation and one atomic settings update. A small\n+machine-local trust-grant ledger records which origin/path keys a CLI or\n+pre-push grant wrote for each canonical worktree. Re-granting after an identity\n+change removes superseded keys from that worktree's prior grant before writing\n+the new identity; revoke removes both the current identity and every key in that\n+record. Hand-authored entries not recorded as a grant are never heuristically\n+deleted. This preserves origin-wide trust while fixing origin-to-path and\n+path-to-origin stale grants. Status reports the exact currently matched trust\n+source.\n \n@@ -377,7 +390,19 @@\n \n-Pre-push never prompts. If an untrusted globally activated repository has no\n-pending checkpoints, the hook emits nothing. If checkpoints are pending, the\n-hook prints one single-line hold notice, returns success, and leaves the user's\n-normal branch push untouched. The notice points to the resolved user settings\n-file instead of an unavailable command.\n+Pre-push preserves the current trust flow. If an untrusted globally activated\n+repository has no pending checkpoints, the hook emits nothing and does not\n+prompt. If checkpoints are pending and a real interactive terminal is\n+available, the hook opens the three-choice trust prompt using `/dev/tty`, never\n+Git's stdin:\n+\n+- \"Yes\" records the current repository identity and drains the queued\n+  checkpoints after re-evaluating policy;\n+- \"Not now\" keeps capturing locally and leaves the queue for a later push; and\n+- \"Always\" records `trust_all`, re-evaluates policy, and drains the queue.\n+\n+If the prompt is unavailable, aborted, or fails—or if persistence or policy\n+re-evaluation fails—the checkpoint queue remains held while the user's normal\n+branch push continues. Accessible mode must use a supported explicit selection\n+path or hold; it must never accept a default implicitly, panic, or consume\n+pre-push stdin. The held message remains actionable and points to `entire trust`\n+and the resolved settings file.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787607977396,"completed_at_ms":1787607977465}}
