{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:55:42.692Z","ordinal":9833,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbddc512087d0b7d865b94c1316e3","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9VmZEezhGko03MAVBOJibnmY","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git log --oneline --decorate --reverse origin/main..HEAD && git log --format='%h%n%B%n---' origin/main..HEAD -- cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go | sed -n '1,520p'\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":30000}); text(r);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787608538.922234}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:55:42.837Z","ordinal":9834,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-897fc39c-f2ca-4069-8d46-026e7cef654b","process_id":"48919","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","git log --oneline --decorate --reverse origin/main..HEAD && git log --format='%h%n%B%n---' origin/main..HEAD -- cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go | sed -n '1,520p'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git log --oneline --decorate --reverse origin/main..HEAD && git log --format='%h%n%B%n---' origin/main..HEAD -- cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go | sed -n '1,520p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"e0d5732cd feat(settings): add user-global settings tier with exclude lists\nceb99f9cc feat(hooks): consult the user-global tier at both hook gates\n42034a2ef feat(hooks): lazy invisible enable for globally tracked repos\n745526e59 fix(global): per-worktree invisible routing + route diagnostics through AbsPath (namespacing portion; diagnostics routing lands in the agent-hooks split, migration scoping in the writer split)\n94ae1fcef feat(enable): global tracking writer — enable/disable --global, ask-once wizard, runtime-data migration\n269289137 fix(global): scope the enable-time runtime-data migration to the current worktree's namespace\n52d47fdee feat(global): user-level agent hooks — install/status/doctor + wrong-folder notice\ncb180a524 fix(global): per-worktree invisible routing + route diagnostics through AbsPath\n802db6efb test(global): derive enable --global flag-conflict coverage; pin redaction configuration under global mode\n6e752cf90 docs(hooks): correct the initHookLogging gate-ordering comment\nc7fb1f6ef fix(settings): trim whitespace in exclude patterns; document remote scope choice\nab7d9f6fc test(settings): pin leading-whitespace tilde pattern expansion\nbe759ce3b Merge feat/global-core fixes forward\n095d66150 Merge feat/global-invisible fixes forward\n98d75792d fix(global): context-aware wizard prompt; isolate git config in worktree test\na68aba05e Merge feat/global-writer fixes forward\nf8c7e9375 fix(global): context-aware removal prompt; user-scope installs skip permissions parse; type-aware flag-conflict test\n68958f183 fix(settings): fail-closed exclusion, symlink-robust path matching, gate tests\n6215560f4 Merge feat/global-core (fail-closed exclusion hardening) into feat/global-invisible\n1be819ab5 Merge feat/global-invisible forward (fail-closed exclusion hardening)\n87d4f1d7d Merge feat/global-writer forward (fail-closed exclusion hardening)\n03cd547fd docs(settings): state the GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract\n51e6787e8 Merge feat/global-invisible forward (GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract)\n142d66329 Merge feat/global-writer forward (GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract)\n1ec6d51f8 feat(doctor): validate global-tracking settings — surface what dead hook logs cannot\nb46a09013 fix(paths,strategy): invisible routing and lazy setup fail toward invisibility\n36e227d10 chore(paths): comment corrections, layout contract export, invariant tests\nb2dd7332a Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\na2206e00e refactor(setup): consume the exported invisible-layout contract\n1ef56897f Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n8da96a889 feat(doctor): explain worktree-resident hooksPath instead of clearing the marker\n84ae1681d fix(lifecycle): unroutable runtime path skips the turn-end capture instead of failing the hook\nfca583b52 Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n7dd63f421 Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\nc38fac9ad chore(doctor): align hooksPath explanation with sibling header style\nde39598ae fix(global): repo-level takeover runs everywhere a settings file is born\nfbde176f3 test(global): pin the writer layer's promises; comment corrections\n332d61e79 Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\nb90de4e82 refactor(settings): nil-safe global accessors, locked user-settings writes, shared pattern check\ne6d4c49a7 fix(global): review fold-ins — consent-race recheck, capped migration warns, actionable gitignore warn\na26b7ac2d Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n22041897c fix(global): verb-scoped hook recognition, atomic writes, and lossless merges for agent settings\n82f6c62c3 fix(global): honest diagnostics — error-aware hook checks, per-repo status truth, doctor probe handling\nf80ac2284 docs(global): correct stale and overbroad comments on the global-tracking surfaces\n2ac3ec1d8 fix(global): residual user-scope writer issues — dangling symlinks, file modes, gemini recognition/completeness, honest repair reporting\n190783286 fix(global): deliver the inactive SessionStart notice through the agent's hook-response channel\ne707f826f docs(global): correct the gemini user-hook no-double-fire mechanism\n5f9f010a4 feat(settings): add exclude_paths_exact and polish the global gate API\nac70fd121 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n4567246e5 fix(hooks): never fail TurnStart/SubagentStart on unroutable runtime paths\nd4a26822d Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\ned6cbc577 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n8da187adf fix(agents): verb-scope repo-level hook recognition for the remaining agents\n182372f73 perf(settings): pin the global gate's no-fork fast path\n4f33d9f48 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n9ae3a994c Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n5dc4f6435 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n39a39ce1b fix(status): render every in-repo inactive reason on the global tracking line\n3f45f68db fix(settings): lock the user-global settings writers at the layer that introduces them\n1d3f451ad Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n9d0531062 fix(global): route diagnostics through AbsPath; settings writers observe their own writes\nd0374492c fix(global): doctor bundle degrades instead of aborting on an unroutable logs path\ne9d2fbfcc fix(global): doctor logs / trace name the routing failure instead of \"not a git repository\"\na6bc064c0 feat(settings): trust schema, RepoTrustIdentity, and the checkpoint egress predicate\n8d65b8273 feat(strategy): hold checkpoint egress for untrusted globally-enrolled repos; y/n/A trust prompt at interactive pushes\nf5fd5b1b3 feat(cli): entire trust command, detection warn, and trust surfaces across status/doctor/session-start\n6b62828c4 docs+test(global): trust-gate docs section and end-to-end held/trusted push coverage\n7ae8dd485 test(global): apply test audit — drop redundant pins, strengthen revoke no-op, cover prompt-error and hand-edit tolerance\nc9e788c67 fix(global): apply toolkit review round — pushurl-aware trust identity, wizard warn ack, inactive-tier refusal, poisoned-path resilience\nd91eeeef7 test(global): enforce the Tests and Comments policy\nc82ffe01f test(global): reduce test volume to the integration-anchored core; strip rationale comments\n0c3bb8158 fix(global): close origin-exclusion fail-open gaps\n3b66859ff fix(gitremote): preserve context cancellation through the repo-ness probe\n04f7bf491 fix(global): guard runtime-data migration against live writers and divergent leftovers\n92b05e182 fix(settings): fail closed on malformed exclude_origins without an origin (D gate shape)\nfd384895c test(global): reduce test volume toward the integration-anchored core\n499e87670 fix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n2b35db349 fix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\ncd7dd8a7b fix(jsonutil): apply the temp file's mode via fd-based chmod before close\n549d1f0c1 fix(gitremote): never swallow a cancellation into \"no origin configured\"\ndad799740 fix(global): fsync the migration copy before removing its source\n03b9b2dec fix(paths): propagate context cancellation through the routing probe\n6e4840470 fix(paths): a cached routing error must not mask the caller's cancellation\n9daa4e6c0 fix(global): bare 'entire' respects the global tier; /.git origins normalize\n7aaeceb70 test(settings): pin Windows drive-letter absolutes through the exclude guard\nd676f4614 fix(global): serialize hook install/remove; harden the bare-entire and exclude guards\nf4423a32c fix(strategy): serialize hook install/remove across processes (B shape)\n98bee6472 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/global-core\n0bffa4822 Merge branch 'feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n400a52283 Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n1a1c5a27e Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n922f4ec57 Merge branch 'feat/global-agent-hooks' into feat/global-trust\n0b22946b6 test(strategy): make the install-lock regression test actually catch the race\n1856d4829 fix(global): don't remove the routed tree if a session activates mid-migration\n56182b440 perf(jsonutil): stop the symlink walk at a self-referential link\n717dc8e65 fix(jsonutil): name both paths when a symlinked write fails\ndadaf9cf2 docs: resolve leftover CLAUDE.md conflict markers from the D merge\nd93594059 Merge origin/main into feat/global-core\na8aa5b281 fix(global): preserve explicit activation intent\nd91860ce9 Merge feat/global-core into feat/global-invisible\n82a3d08da fix(strategy): document best-effort setup skip\n730a1763a Merge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n1152c3dd3 Merge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n1e753a46f Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n922f9f18e fix(global): require Claude subagent stop user hook\ne22e39f2f Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n3e76fbba9 fix(settings): enforce trusted activation intent\n5e89a4bfe Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\ncd861285d fix(paths): keep tracked local activation invisible\n31e7cd5c7 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n593d526a9 fix(global): avoid overwriting live migration data\n8bd406e5b Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n2ba044d30 fix(claude): verify every user lifecycle hook\n92f40315b fix(paths): preserve activation under cancellation\n5a85aed6f fix(global): serialize hooks with runtime migration\n875b2d746 fix(hooks): log inactive response failures\nd749591c6 merge: propagate global enable stack fixes\n5144d12d4 (origin/feat/global-core, feat/global-core) perf(settings): fold exclusion paths once\n66e2c6e70 merge: propagate exclusion matching fix\n5e61e13bc merge: propagate global enable fixes\neec513577 merge: propagate global enable fixes\nf099212da merge: propagate global enable fixes\n646585363 (origin/feat/global-invisible, feat/global-invisible) fix(paths): stop invisible fallbacks on cancellation\nd1493af16 Merge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n0201d7f7e (origin/feat/global-agent-hooks, feat/global-agent-hooks) Merge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\nfd60aa12e Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\na92031b1b (origin/feat/global-writer, feat/global-writer) fix: harden global runtime takeover\n3d1874fe3 merge: consolidate global enable stack\nbca00205a (HEAD -> fix/global-takeover-migration, origin/feat/global-trust, feat/global-trust) merge: integrate current main into global enable\n3d1874fe3\nmerge: consolidate global enable stack\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0TPDDEDFB3YH22Y1Q7BYMBD\n\n---\na92031b1b\nfix: harden global runtime takeover\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0TMAK37EEM2MHT8XMYGK0AF\n\n---\nfd60aa12e\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\n---\n0201d7f7e\nMerge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n---\nd1493af16\nMerge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n\n---\n646585363\nfix(paths): stop invisible fallbacks on cancellation\n\n---\nf099212da\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\neec513577\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\n5e61e13bc\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\n66e2c6e70\nmerge: propagate exclusion matching fix\n\n---\n5144d12d4\nperf(settings): fold exclusion paths once\n\n---\nd749591c6\nmerge: propagate global enable stack fixes\n\n---\n875b2d746\nfix(hooks): log inactive response failures\n\n---\n5a85aed6f\nfix(global): serialize hooks with runtime migration\n\n---\n92f40315b\nfix(paths): preserve activation under cancellation\n\n---\n2ba044d30\nfix(claude): verify every user lifecycle hook\n\n---\n8bd406e5b\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n---\n593d526a9\nfix(global): avoid overwriting live migration data\n\n---\n31e7cd5c7\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n---\ncd861285d\nfix(paths): keep tracked local activation invisible\n\n---\ne22e39f2f\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\nCarry the Claude SubagentStop user-hook completeness repair into the final trust-gate branch.\n\n---\n922f9f18e\nfix(global): require Claude subagent stop user hook\n\nKeep user-level completeness aligned with repo-level freshness so a partial install is detected and repaired.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0JSMPDC8WGT2616NAP2J95X\n\n---\n1e753a46f\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\nCarry explicit repo activation intent through checkpoint egress, trust commands, and status. Incidental settings continue through the global trust gate; malformed activation settings hold data locally.\n\n---\n1152c3dd3\nMerge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\nCarry explicit repo activation intent through status reasons and user-level hook coverage. Preserve the safer user-settings writer while integrating Claude Code SubagentStop support.\n\n---\n730a1763a\nMerge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n\nCarry explicit activation-intent semantics through first-run setup, repo takeover, and user-global writes.\n\n---\n82a3d08da\nfix(strategy): document best-effort setup skip\n\n---\nd91860ce9\nMerge feat/global-core into feat/global-invisible\n\nPreserve explicit activation-intent semantics in invisible runtime routing and lazy hook setup.\n\n---\na8aa5b281\nfix(global): preserve explicit activation intent\n\n---\n1856d4829\nfix(global): don't remove the routed tree if a session activates mid-migration\n\nTrail 1014 finding on the TOCTOU window between the active-session check\nand the moves. The window is real and cannot be closed from this side:\nhook runtime-data writes (lifecycle's prompt.txt and full.jsonl) take no\nlock, so a migration-side lock would only serialize concurrent enables.\nWhat CAN be narrowed is the damage — re-check after the moves and skip\ndirectory removal, the one remaining destructive step, which is what\nturns a live hook's write into ENOENT. Leftovers cost only a later\nsweep: a non-empty routed dir re-triggers migration on the next enable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n922f4ec57\nMerge branch 'feat/global-agent-hooks' into feat/global-trust\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tCLAUDE.md\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go\n\n---\n1a1c5a27e\nMerge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/hooks_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/factoryaidroid/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go\n\n---\n400a52283\nMerge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/setup.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go\n\n---\n0bffa4822\nMerge branch 'feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks_test.go\n\n---\nd676f4614\nfix(global): serialize hook install/remove; harden the bare-entire and exclude guards\n\nTrail 1012 findings:\n\n- Concurrent first-install race (HIGH): global mode moves first-ever git\n  hook installation into hook processes that fire concurrently, and the\n  unsynchronized read→rename→write could rename a half-installed wrapper\n  over the user's hook backup — destroying the hook and leaving a\n  wrapper chaining to itself. InstallGitHook and RemoveGitHook now take\n  a cross-process flock in the git common dir (never the hooks dir,\n  which can be worktree-resident). Regression test mutation-verified:\n  fails on the unlocked code with the exact self-chain corruption.\n- Bare 'entire' no longer treats an UNUSABLE global config as \"tier says\n  no\": the gate reads the enabled bit itself — an unreadable settings\n  file gets a stderr warning instead of a wizard that would pin the repo\n  out of the tier, and a tier-enabled-but-excluded repo is not funneled\n  into repo-level setup either.\n- expandTilde accepts only filepath.IsAbs patterns: the leading-slash\n  allowance was redundant on Unix and fail-open on Windows, where the\n  MSYS spelling /c/code/** can never match a drive-rooted root.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n6e4840470\nfix(paths): a cached routing error must not mask the caller's cancellation\n\nTrail 1013 finding: the memo's hit path returned a cached\nErrUnroutableRuntimePath to callers arriving with an already-canceled\ncontext, misreporting their cancellation as a routing failure. A cached\nerror now yields the cancellation instead; a cached BASE is still served\n— the memo read needs no I/O, and teardown paths may resolve paths under\nan already-canceled context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n03b9b2dec\nfix(paths): propagate context cancellation through the routing probe\n\nTrail 1013 finding: a canceled context failing the git-common-dir probe\nwas wrapped as ErrUnroutableRuntimePath, turning a dying process's\ncancellation into the callers' silent skip; propagate the cancellation\ninstead (same fix as gitremote's repo-ness probe). Also never cache a\ncancellation-tainted result — the memo would otherwise poison every\nlater resolution in the process with the stale cancellation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\ndad799740\nfix(global): fsync the migration copy before removing its source\n\nTrail 1014 finding: copyFileThenRemove renamed and then deleted the\nsource without syncing the temp file, so a crash could surface the\nrename with the bytes still in cache — losing the file outright since\nthe source is already gone. Sync before close, matching WriteFileAtomic.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n2b35db349\nfix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n\nTrail 1016 findings: mirrors feat/global-core's 499e87670 into this\nbranch's copy of the gate (identical hunks for the landing merge), and\nadds two clarifying doc lines the same review asked after — ensureHook's\nshared snapshot cannot overcount (every call checks a distinct\nmatcher/command pair), and resolveWriteTarget keeps relative paths\nrelative (EvalSymlinks never absolutizes).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n499e87670\nfix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n\nTrail 1016 finding: prefer Match over the ValidatePattern+MatchUnvalidated\npairing so the matching call itself can never run an assumed-valid pattern;\nthe ValidatePattern pass stays for the no-origin vet path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n92b05e182\nfix(settings): fail closed on malformed exclude_origins without an origin (D gate shape)\n\nMirrors feat/global-core's 0c3bb8158 into this branch's rewrite of the\ngate: computeGlobalModeStatus vets the exclude_origins list before the\norigin lookup, and matchesExcludeOrigin validates every pattern even\nwith an empty origin — this branch's version of the function supersedes\nthe base's at landing, so it must carry the same fail-closed behavior.\nText mirrors the base commit so the landing merge sees identical hunks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n04f7bf491\nfix(global): guard runtime-data migration against live writers and divergent leftovers\n\nTrail 1014 findings on maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData:\n\n- A destination file that already exists is dropped from the source only\n  when its content is identical; a divergent or uncomparable pair now\n  counts as failed — into the summary's 'left in <source>' bucket — where\n  a blind skip previously stranded the source under .git silently and\n  forever.\n- Migration defers (with a printed re-run hint) when a session is ACTIVE\n  in this worktree: a hook process may be mid-write under the routed dir,\n  where a rename strands its in-flight file and the EXDEV copy fallback\n  can snapshot a half-written one. Idle sessions and other worktrees'\n  sessions don't defer. The non-empty routed dir re-triggers migration on\n  the next enable, which is the documented recovery point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n0c3bb8158\nfix(global): close origin-exclusion fail-open gaps\n\nReview findings on trail 1012:\n\n- splitOwnerRepo sheds trailing slashes and any-case \".git\", so a stored\n  origin like https://github.com/acme/widgets/ normalizes to\n  github.com/acme/widgets instead of a form no exclude pattern matches\n  (fail-open), and every ParseURL caller stops seeing \"widgets/\" repos.\n- matchesExcludeOrigin validates every pattern even without an origin, and\n  GlobalModeActive vets the list before the origin lookup, so a malformed\n  exclude_origins entry fails closed identically whether or not the repo\n  has an origin.\n- GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet reports a blank 'url =' value as found=true with\n  the empty value (the gate fails closed on it) and errors on a non-repo\n  dir instead of misreading git's scope-fallback exit 1 as \"no origin\n  configured\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nc82ffe01f\ntest(global): reduce test volume to the integration-anchored core; strip rationale comments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nc9e788c67\nfix(global): apply toolkit review round — pushurl-aware trust identity, wizard warn ack, inactive-tier refusal, poisoned-path resilience\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nf5fd5b1b3\nfeat(cli): entire trust command, detection warn, and trust surfaces across status/doctor/session-start\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M08T1GNCGPYG9T71HPB70R9S\n\n---\n8d65b8273\nfeat(strategy): hold checkpoint egress for untrusted globally-enrolled repos; y/n/A trust prompt at interactive pushes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\na6bc064c0\nfeat(settings): trust schema, RepoTrustIdentity, and the checkpoint egress predicate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n9d0531062\nfix(global): route diagnostics through AbsPath; settings writers observe their own writes\n\nFixes both open trail findings on this layer:\n\n- 019ff8ab-9a2: doctor bundle/logs/trace built log paths as\n  filepath.Join(repoRoot, logging.LogsDir), silently producing empty\n  diagnostics for globally tracked repos (addDirToZip skips a missing\n  dir without error; doctor logs reports \"No log file\"). All three now\n  resolve through paths.AbsPath, with one routed-logs test per command.\n  Ported verbatim from the agent-hooks layer upstack so the merge-up\n  stays content-identical.\n\n- 019ff8ab-97d: the invisibleCache comment claimed the enable/disable\n  layers already call ClearInvisibleRuntimeCache, but nothing at this\n  layer did: `entire enable` latches the pre-write routing decision\n  (logging.Init resolves .entire/logs before settings.json exists) for\n  the rest of the process. saveRaw/saveToFile now clear the cache after\n  every write (ported from the writer layer upstack, which keeps its\n  identical hunks), and the comment now states what holds at this layer.\n  TestRepoSettingsWrites_ClearInvisibleRoutingCache pins the contract;\n  the upstack copy in global_save_test.go supersedes it on merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n3f45f68db\nfix(settings): lock the user-global settings writers at the layer that introduces them\n\nAll three writers (enable --global, disable --global, the wizard prompt) did\nan unlocked load-modify-save of ~/.config/entire/settings.json; the wizard's\npre-persist re-check only narrowed its race. ModifyUserSettings now runs the\ncycle under the same flock pattern used for clone preferences, the wizard's\nsupersede check moves inside the locked callback, and SaveUserSettings\ndelegates so no unlocked write path remains. The upstack layer carries the\nsame shape; this puts the lock in the PR where the writers are born so the\nstack never merges an unlocked window onto main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n5dc4f6435\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\n9ae3a994c\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\n4f33d9f48\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n\n---\n182372f73\nperf(settings): pin the global gate's no-fork fast path\n\nReview of the stack tip caught the memoized gate variant resolving\npaths.WorktreeRoot — a git rev-parse subprocess fork — before the cheap\nnil/disabled settings check, taxing every hook invocation in every repo\nwithout repo-level setup even when the global tier is unconfigured (the\nmachine-wide common case). This layer's GlobalModeActive already checks\nsettings first; make that ordering a stated invariant (doc comment),\nroute the resolution through a worktreeRootFn seam, and add a test that\nfails if the unconfigured/disabled path ever resolves the root. The\nmemoized variants upstack are reordered to satisfy the same test as the\nstack re-merges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n8da187adf\nfix(agents): verb-scope repo-level hook recognition for the remaining agents\n\nPropagate the verb-scoped recognizer this round shipped for claude-code\nand gemini at user scope to the four agents that still matched managed\nhooks by the bare 'entire ' prefix at repo scope: codex, cursor,\ncopilot-cli, and factoryai-droid. A user-authored hook that merely\ninvokes the entire CLI (e.g. 'entire status --json > /tmp/s.json') was\nrecognized as ours and destroyed on uninstall or force reinstall. Every\nprefix is now scoped to '... hooks ', and every legacy local-dev form an\nolder installer wrote (unquoted then quoted rev-parse go-run) is\nretained verb-scoped. opencode and pi recognize their generated file by\na whole-file marker, not command prefixes — unchanged. Per-agent tests\npin that a user-authored entire-CLI hook survives force install and\nuninstall.\n\nAlso from review of this layer:\n- add the missing test seam for doctor's probe-error branch\n  (SetHooksDirProbeErrorForTesting) and pin that checkGlobalTracking\n  prints GIT HOOK STATE UNVERIFIED without clearing the\n  global_setup_completed marker when the residency probe fails\n- refactor ValidateGlobalConfig into pure ValidateGlobalPatterns over\n  the loaded config plus a thin loading wrapper, and pass the loaded\n  config into UnnormalizableOrigins — doctor loaded the settings file\n  three times per run; it now loads once. exclude_paths_exact entries\n  are validated too (tilde-expansion only; they are not globs)\n- record the third-agent availability-gate contract on the User-Level\n  Hook Support checklist section (trail 968 finding 019fef03-2ad1)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\ned6cbc577\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\nd4a26822d\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/paths/entire_join_guard_test.go\n\n---\n4567246e5\nfix(hooks): never fail TurnStart/SubagentStart on unroutable runtime paths\n\nThree invisible-tracking fixes from review:\n\nTurnStart and SubagentStart propagated paths.ErrUnroutableRuntimePath\nfrom CapturePrePromptState/CapturePreTaskState straight out of the hook,\nexiting non-zero on every prompt in a globally tracked repo whose\ngit-side location cannot be resolved — violating the sentinel's own\n'never fail the user's operation' contract and contradicting turn-end,\nwhich already skips. Both handlers now mirror the turn-end pattern:\nWarn (pre-state capture skipped this turn) and continue, keeping\nstate.go's 'callers skip' contract true. Attribution safety when the\nbaseline is skipped: in the steady unroutable state turn-end skips\ncheckpoint capture entirely before attribution; only an asymmetric\ntransient failure reaches the nil-preState path, which is the\nlong-standing no-TurnStart behavior shared with exec-mode agents.\n\nEnsurePrimaryRef wrote five ✓ bootstrap notices unconditionally to\nos.Stderr, leaking into agent hook output (observed live). The writer\nis now threaded through (EnsurePrimaryRefTo/createOrphanMetadataRef);\nhook-context callers — MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup and EnsureSetupForHook's\nensureSetup — pass io.Discard, while interactive flows (enable, agent\nsetup) keep os.Stderr via the unchanged EnsurePrimaryRef/EnsureSetup\nentry points.\n\nTestNoDirectEntireJoins' allowlist was file-scoped; it now requires an\ninline '// entire-join-ok: <reason>' marker per call site, so a new\nbypass in an already-audited file is still flagged and deleting a\nmarker re-flags its site (mutation-verified).\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"e0d5732cd feat(settings): add user-global settings tier with exclude lists\nceb99f9cc feat(hooks): consult the user-global tier at both hook gates\n42034a2ef feat(hooks): lazy invisible enable for globally tracked repos\n745526e59 fix(global): per-worktree invisible routing + route diagnostics through AbsPath (namespacing portion; diagnostics routing lands in the agent-hooks split, migration scoping in the writer split)\n94ae1fcef feat(enable): global tracking writer — enable/disable --global, ask-once wizard, runtime-data migration\n269289137 fix(global): scope the enable-time runtime-data migration to the current worktree's namespace\n52d47fdee feat(global): user-level agent hooks — install/status/doctor + wrong-folder notice\ncb180a524 fix(global): per-worktree invisible routing + route diagnostics through AbsPath\n802db6efb test(global): derive enable --global flag-conflict coverage; pin redaction configuration under global mode\n6e752cf90 docs(hooks): correct the initHookLogging gate-ordering comment\nc7fb1f6ef fix(settings): trim whitespace in exclude patterns; document remote scope choice\nab7d9f6fc test(settings): pin leading-whitespace tilde pattern expansion\nbe759ce3b Merge feat/global-core fixes forward\n095d66150 Merge feat/global-invisible fixes forward\n98d75792d fix(global): context-aware wizard prompt; isolate git config in worktree test\na68aba05e Merge feat/global-writer fixes forward\nf8c7e9375 fix(global): context-aware removal prompt; user-scope installs skip permissions parse; type-aware flag-conflict test\n68958f183 fix(settings): fail-closed exclusion, symlink-robust path matching, gate tests\n6215560f4 Merge feat/global-core (fail-closed exclusion hardening) into feat/global-invisible\n1be819ab5 Merge feat/global-invisible forward (fail-closed exclusion hardening)\n87d4f1d7d Merge feat/global-writer forward (fail-closed exclusion hardening)\n03cd547fd docs(settings): state the GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract\n51e6787e8 Merge feat/global-invisible forward (GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract)\n142d66329 Merge feat/global-writer forward (GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract)\n1ec6d51f8 feat(doctor): validate global-tracking settings — surface what dead hook logs cannot\nb46a09013 fix(paths,strategy): invisible routing and lazy setup fail toward invisibility\n36e227d10 chore(paths): comment corrections, layout contract export, invariant tests\nb2dd7332a Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\na2206e00e refactor(setup): consume the exported invisible-layout contract\n1ef56897f Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n8da96a889 feat(doctor): explain worktree-resident hooksPath instead of clearing the marker\n84ae1681d fix(lifecycle): unroutable runtime path skips the turn-end capture instead of failing the hook\nfca583b52 Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n7dd63f421 Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\nc38fac9ad chore(doctor): align hooksPath explanation with sibling header style\nde39598ae fix(global): repo-level takeover runs everywhere a settings file is born\nfbde176f3 test(global): pin the writer layer's promises; comment corrections\n332d61e79 Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\nb90de4e82 refactor(settings): nil-safe global accessors, locked user-settings writes, shared pattern check\ne6d4c49a7 fix(global): review fold-ins — consent-race recheck, capped migration warns, actionable gitignore warn\na26b7ac2d Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n22041897c fix(global): verb-scoped hook recognition, atomic writes, and lossless merges for agent settings\n82f6c62c3 fix(global): honest diagnostics — error-aware hook checks, per-repo status truth, doctor probe handling\nf80ac2284 docs(global): correct stale and overbroad comments on the global-tracking surfaces\n2ac3ec1d8 fix(global): residual user-scope writer issues — dangling symlinks, file modes, gemini recognition/completeness, honest repair reporting\n190783286 fix(global): deliver the inactive SessionStart notice through the agent's hook-response channel\ne707f826f docs(global): correct the gemini user-hook no-double-fire mechanism\n5f9f010a4 feat(settings): add exclude_paths_exact and polish the global gate API\nac70fd121 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n4567246e5 fix(hooks): never fail TurnStart/SubagentStart on unroutable runtime paths\nd4a26822d Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\ned6cbc577 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n8da187adf fix(agents): verb-scope repo-level hook recognition for the remaining agents\n182372f73 perf(settings): pin the global gate's no-fork fast path\n4f33d9f48 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n9ae3a994c Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n5dc4f6435 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n39a39ce1b fix(status): render every in-repo inactive reason on the global tracking line\n3f45f68db fix(settings): lock the user-global settings writers at the layer that introduces them\n1d3f451ad Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n9d0531062 fix(global): route diagnostics through AbsPath; settings writers observe their own writes\nd0374492c fix(global): doctor bundle degrades instead of aborting on an unroutable logs path\ne9d2fbfcc fix(global): doctor logs / trace name the routing failure instead of \"not a git repository\"\na6bc064c0 feat(settings): trust schema, RepoTrustIdentity, and the checkpoint egress predicate\n8d65b8273 feat(strategy): hold checkpoint egress for untrusted globally-enrolled repos; y/n/A trust prompt at interactive pushes\nf5fd5b1b3 feat(cli): entire trust command, detection warn, and trust surfaces across status/doctor/session-start\n6b62828c4 docs+test(global): trust-gate docs section and end-to-end held/trusted push coverage\n7ae8dd485 test(global): apply test audit — drop redundant pins, strengthen revoke no-op, cover prompt-error and hand-edit tolerance\nc9e788c67 fix(global): apply toolkit review round — pushurl-aware trust identity, wizard warn ack, inactive-tier refusal, poisoned-path resilience\nd91eeeef7 test(global): enforce the Tests and Comments policy\nc82ffe01f test(global): reduce test volume to the integration-anchored core; strip rationale comments\n0c3bb8158 fix(global): close origin-exclusion fail-open gaps\n3b66859ff fix(gitremote): preserve context cancellation through the repo-ness probe\n04f7bf491 fix(global): guard runtime-data migration against live writers and divergent leftovers\n92b05e182 fix(settings): fail closed on malformed exclude_origins without an origin (D gate shape)\nfd384895c test(global): reduce test volume toward the integration-anchored core\n499e87670 fix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n2b35db349 fix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\ncd7dd8a7b fix(jsonutil): apply the temp file's mode via fd-based chmod before close\n549d1f0c1 fix(gitremote): never swallow a cancellation into \"no origin configured\"\ndad799740 fix(global): fsync the migration copy before removing its source\n03b9b2dec fix(paths): propagate context cancellation through the routing probe\n6e4840470 fix(paths): a cached routing error must not mask the caller's cancellation\n9daa4e6c0 fix(global): bare 'entire' respects the global tier; /.git origins normalize\n7aaeceb70 test(settings): pin Windows drive-letter absolutes through the exclude guard\nd676f4614 fix(global): serialize hook install/remove; harden the bare-entire and exclude guards\nf4423a32c fix(strategy): serialize hook install/remove across processes (B shape)\n98bee6472 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/global-core\n0bffa4822 Merge branch 'feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n400a52283 Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n1a1c5a27e Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n922f4ec57 Merge branch 'feat/global-agent-hooks' into feat/global-trust\n0b22946b6 test(strategy): make the install-lock regression test actually catch the race\n1856d4829 fix(global): don't remove the routed tree if a session activates mid-migration\n56182b440 perf(jsonutil): stop the symlink walk at a self-referential link\n717dc8e65 fix(jsonutil): name both paths when a symlinked write fails\ndadaf9cf2 docs: resolve leftover CLAUDE.md conflict markers from the D merge\nd93594059 Merge origin/main into feat/global-core\na8aa5b281 fix(global): preserve explicit activation intent\nd91860ce9 Merge feat/global-core into feat/global-invisible\n82a3d08da fix(strategy): document best-effort setup skip\n730a1763a Merge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n1152c3dd3 Merge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n1e753a46f Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n922f9f18e fix(global): require Claude subagent stop user hook\ne22e39f2f Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n3e76fbba9 fix(settings): enforce trusted activation intent\n5e89a4bfe Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\ncd861285d fix(paths): keep tracked local activation invisible\n31e7cd5c7 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n593d526a9 fix(global): avoid overwriting live migration data\n8bd406e5b Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n2ba044d30 fix(claude): verify every user lifecycle hook\n92f40315b fix(paths): preserve activation under cancellation\n5a85aed6f fix(global): serialize hooks with runtime migration\n875b2d746 fix(hooks): log inactive response failures\nd749591c6 merge: propagate global enable stack fixes\n5144d12d4 (origin/feat/global-core, feat/global-core) perf(settings): fold exclusion paths once\n66e2c6e70 merge: propagate exclusion matching fix\n5e61e13bc merge: propagate global enable fixes\neec513577 merge: propagate global enable fixes\nf099212da merge: propagate global enable fixes\n646585363 (origin/feat/global-invisible, feat/global-invisible) fix(paths): stop invisible fallbacks on cancellation\nd1493af16 Merge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n0201d7f7e (origin/feat/global-agent-hooks, feat/global-agent-hooks) Merge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\nfd60aa12e Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\na92031b1b (origin/feat/global-writer, feat/global-writer) fix: harden global runtime takeover\n3d1874fe3 merge: consolidate global enable stack\nbca00205a (HEAD -> fix/global-takeover-migration, origin/feat/global-trust, feat/global-trust) merge: integrate current main into global enable\n3d1874fe3\nmerge: consolidate global enable stack\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0TPDDEDFB3YH22Y1Q7BYMBD\n\n---\na92031b1b\nfix: harden global runtime takeover\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0TMAK37EEM2MHT8XMYGK0AF\n\n---\nfd60aa12e\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\n---\n0201d7f7e\nMerge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n---\nd1493af16\nMerge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n\n---\n646585363\nfix(paths): stop invisible fallbacks on cancellation\n\n---\nf099212da\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\neec513577\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\n5e61e13bc\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\n66e2c6e70\nmerge: propagate exclusion matching fix\n\n---\n5144d12d4\nperf(settings): fold exclusion paths once\n\n---\nd749591c6\nmerge: propagate global enable stack fixes\n\n---\n875b2d746\nfix(hooks): log inactive response failures\n\n---\n5a85aed6f\nfix(global): serialize hooks with runtime migration\n\n---\n92f40315b\nfix(paths): preserve activation under cancellation\n\n---\n2ba044d30\nfix(claude): verify every user lifecycle hook\n\n---\n8bd406e5b\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n---\n593d526a9\nfix(global): avoid overwriting live migration data\n\n---\n31e7cd5c7\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n---\ncd861285d\nfix(paths): keep tracked local activation invisible\n\n---\ne22e39f2f\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\nCarry the Claude SubagentStop user-hook completeness repair into the final trust-gate branch.\n\n---\n922f9f18e\nfix(global): require Claude subagent stop user hook\n\nKeep user-level completeness aligned with repo-level freshness so a partial install is detected and repaired.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0JSMPDC8WGT2616NAP2J95X\n\n---\n1e753a46f\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\nCarry explicit repo activation intent through checkpoint egress, trust commands, and status. Incidental settings continue through the global trust gate; malformed activation settings hold data locally.\n\n---\n1152c3dd3\nMerge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\nCarry explicit repo activation intent through status reasons and user-level hook coverage. Preserve the safer user-settings writer while integrating Claude Code SubagentStop support.\n\n---\n730a1763a\nMerge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n\nCarry explicit activation-intent semantics through first-run setup, repo takeover, and user-global writes.\n\n---\n82a3d08da\nfix(strategy): document best-effort setup skip\n\n---\nd91860ce9\nMerge feat/global-core into feat/global-invisible\n\nPreserve explicit activation-intent semantics in invisible runtime routing and lazy hook setup.\n\n---\na8aa5b281\nfix(global): preserve explicit activation intent\n\n---\n1856d4829\nfix(global): don't remove the routed tree if a session activates mid-migration\n\nTrail 1014 finding on the TOCTOU window between the active-session check\nand the moves. The window is real and cannot be closed from this side:\nhook runtime-data writes (lifecycle's prompt.txt and full.jsonl) take no\nlock, so a migration-side lock would only serialize concurrent enables.\nWhat CAN be narrowed is the damage — re-check after the moves and skip\ndirectory removal, the one remaining destructive step, which is what\nturns a live hook's write into ENOENT. Leftovers cost only a later\nsweep: a non-empty routed dir re-triggers migration on the next enable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n922f4ec57\nMerge branch 'feat/global-agent-hooks' into feat/global-trust\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tCLAUDE.md\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go\n\n---\n1a1c5a27e\nMerge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/hooks_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/factoryaidroid/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go\n\n---\n400a52283\nMerge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/setup.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go\n\n---\n0bffa4822\nMerge branch 'feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks_test.go\n\n---\nd676f4614\nfix(global): serialize hook install/remove; harden the bare-entire and exclude guards\n\nTrail 1012 findings:\n\n- Concurrent first-install race (HIGH): global mode moves first-ever git\n  hook installation into hook processes that fire concurrently, and the\n  unsynchronized read→rename→write could rename a half-installed wrapper\n  over the user's hook backup — destroying the hook and leaving a\n  wrapper chaining to itself. InstallGitHook and RemoveGitHook now take\n  a cross-process flock in the git common dir (never the hooks dir,\n  which can be worktree-resident). Regression test mutation-verified:\n  fails on the unlocked code with the exact self-chain corruption.\n- Bare 'entire' no longer treats an UNUSABLE global config as \"tier says\n  no\": the gate reads the enabled bit itself — an unreadable settings\n  file gets a stderr warning instead of a wizard that would pin the repo\n  out of the tier, and a tier-enabled-but-excluded repo is not funneled\n  into repo-level setup either.\n- expandTilde accepts only filepath.IsAbs patterns: the leading-slash\n  allowance was redundant on Unix and fail-open on Windows, where the\n  MSYS spelling /c/code/** can never match a drive-rooted root.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n6e4840470\nfix(paths): a cached routing error must not mask the caller's cancellation\n\nTrail 1013 finding: the memo's hit path returned a cached\nErrUnroutableRuntimePath to callers arriving with an already-canceled\ncontext, misreporting their cancellation as a routing failure. A cached\nerror now yields the cancellation instead; a cached BASE is still served\n— the memo read needs no I/O, and teardown paths may resolve paths under\nan already-canceled context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n03b9b2dec\nfix(paths): propagate context cancellation through the routing probe\n\nTrail 1013 finding: a canceled context failing the git-common-dir probe\nwas wrapped as ErrUnroutableRuntimePath, turning a dying process's\ncancellation into the callers' silent skip; propagate the cancellation\ninstead (same fix as gitremote's repo-ness probe). Also never cache a\ncancellation-tainted result — the memo would otherwise poison every\nlater resolution in the process with the stale cancellation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\ndad799740\nfix(global): fsync the migration copy before removing its source\n\nTrail 1014 finding: copyFileThenRemove renamed and then deleted the\nsource without syncing the temp file, so a crash could surface the\nrename with the bytes still in cache — losing the file outright since\nthe source is already gone. Sync before close, matching WriteFileAtomic.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n2b35db349\nfix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n\nTrail 1016 findings: mirrors feat/global-core's 499e87670 into this\nbranch's copy of the gate (identical hunks for the landing merge), and\nadds two clarifying doc lines the same review asked after — ensureHook's\nshared snapshot cannot overcount (every call checks a distinct\nmatcher/command pair), and resolveWriteTarget keeps relative paths\nrelative (EvalSymlinks never absolutizes).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n499e87670\nfix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n\nTrail 1016 finding: prefer Match over the ValidatePattern+MatchUnvalidated\npairing so the matching call itself can never run an assumed-valid pattern;\nthe ValidatePattern pass stays for the no-origin vet path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n92b05e182\nfix(settings): fail closed on malformed exclude_origins without an origin (D gate shape)\n\nMirrors feat/global-core's 0c3bb8158 into this branch's rewrite of the\ngate: computeGlobalModeStatus vets the exclude_origins list before the\norigin lookup, and matchesExcludeOrigin validates every pattern even\nwith an empty origin — this branch's version of the function supersedes\nthe base's at landing, so it must carry the same fail-closed behavior.\nText mirrors the base commit so the landing merge sees identical hunks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n04f7bf491\nfix(global): guard runtime-data migration against live writers and divergent leftovers\n\nTrail 1014 findings on maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData:\n\n- A destination file that already exists is dropped from the source only\n  when its content is identical; a divergent or uncomparable pair now\n  counts as failed — into the summary's 'left in <source>' bucket — where\n  a blind skip previously stranded the source under .git silently and\n  forever.\n- Migration defers (with a printed re-run hint) when a session is ACTIVE\n  in this worktree: a hook process may be mid-write under the routed dir,\n  where a rename strands its in-flight file and the EXDEV copy fallback\n  can snapshot a half-written one. Idle sessions and other worktrees'\n  sessions don't defer. The non-empty routed dir re-triggers migration on\n  the next enable, which is the documented recovery point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n0c3bb8158\nfix(global): close origin-exclusion fail-open gaps\n\nReview findings on trail 1012:\n\n- splitOwnerRepo sheds trailing slashes and any-case \".git\", so a stored\n  origin like https://github.com/acme/widgets/ normalizes to\n  github.com/acme/widgets instead of a form no exclude pattern matches\n  (fail-open), and every ParseURL caller stops seeing \"widgets/\" repos.\n- matchesExcludeOrigin validates every pattern even without an origin, and\n  GlobalModeActive vets the list before the origin lookup, so a malformed\n  exclude_origins entry fails closed identically whether or not the repo\n  has an origin.\n- GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet reports a blank 'url =' value as found=true with\n  the empty value (the gate fails closed on it) and errors on a non-repo\n  dir instead of misreading git's scope-fallback exit 1 as \"no origin\n  configured\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nc82ffe01f\ntest(global): reduce test volume to the integration-anchored core; strip rationale comments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nc9e788c67\nfix(global): apply toolkit review round — pushurl-aware trust identity, wizard warn ack, inactive-tier refusal, poisoned-path resilience\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nf5fd5b1b3\nfeat(cli): entire trust command, detection warn, and trust surfaces across status/doctor/session-start\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M08T1GNCGPYG9T71HPB70R9S\n\n---\n8d65b8273\nfeat(strategy): hold checkpoint egress for untrusted globally-enrolled repos; y/n/A trust prompt at interactive pushes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\na6bc064c0\nfeat(settings): trust schema, RepoTrustIdentity, and the checkpoint egress predicate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n9d0531062\nfix(global): route diagnostics through AbsPath; settings writers observe their own writes\n\nFixes both open trail findings on this layer:\n\n- 019ff8ab-9a2: doctor bundle/logs/trace built log paths as\n  filepath.Join(repoRoot, logging.LogsDir), silently producing empty\n  diagnostics for globally tracked repos (addDirToZip skips a missing\n  dir without error; doctor logs reports \"No log file\"). All three now\n  resolve through paths.AbsPath, with one routed-logs test per command.\n  Ported verbatim from the agent-hooks layer upstack so the merge-up\n  stays content-identical.\n\n- 019ff8ab-97d: the invisibleCache comment claimed the enable/disable\n  layers already call ClearInvisibleRuntimeCache, but nothing at this\n  layer did: `entire enable` latches the pre-write routing decision\n  (logging.Init resolves .entire/logs before settings.json exists) for\n  the rest of the process. saveRaw/saveToFile now clear the cache after\n  every write (ported from the writer layer upstack, which keeps its\n  identical hunks), and the comment now states what holds at this layer.\n  TestRepoSettingsWrites_ClearInvisibleRoutingCache pins the contract;\n  the upstack copy in global_save_test.go supersedes it on merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n3f45f68db\nfix(settings): lock the user-global settings writers at the layer that introduces them\n\nAll three writers (enable --global, disable --global, the wizard prompt) did\nan unlocked load-modify-save of ~/.config/entire/settings.json; the wizard's\npre-persist re-check only narrowed its race. ModifyUserSettings now runs the\ncycle under the same flock pattern used for clone preferences, the wizard's\nsupersede check moves inside the locked callback, and SaveUserSettings\ndelegates so no unlocked write path remains. The upstack layer carries the\nsame shape; this puts the lock in the PR where the writers are born so the\nstack never merges an unlocked window onto main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n5dc4f6435\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\n9ae3a994c\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\n4f33d9f48\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n\n---\n182372f73\nperf(settings): pin the global gate's no-fork fast path\n\nReview of the stack tip caught the memoized gate variant resolving\npaths.WorktreeRoot — a git rev-parse subprocess fork — before the cheap\nnil/disabled settings check, taxing every hook invocation in every repo\nwithout repo-level setup even when the global tier is unconfigured (the\nmachine-wide common case). This layer's GlobalModeActive already checks\nsettings first; make that ordering a stated invariant (doc comment),\nroute the resolution through a worktreeRootFn seam, and add a test that\nfails if the unconfigured/disabled path ever resolves the root. The\nmemoized variants upstack are reordered to satisfy the same test as the\nstack re-merges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n8da187adf\nfix(agents): verb-scope repo-level hook recognition for the remaining agents\n\nPropagate the verb-scoped recognizer this round shipped for claude-code\nand gemini at user scope to the four agents that still matched managed\nhooks by the bare 'entire ' prefix at repo scope: codex, cursor,\ncopilot-cli, and factoryai-droid. A user-authored hook that merely\ninvokes the entire CLI (e.g. 'entire status --json > /tmp/s.json') was\nrecognized as ours and destroyed on uninstall or force reinstall. Every\nprefix is now scoped to '... hooks ', and every legacy local-dev form an\nolder installer wrote (unquoted then quoted rev-parse go-run) is\nretained verb-scoped. opencode and pi recognize their generated file by\na whole-file marker, not command prefixes — unchanged. Per-agent tests\npin that a user-authored entire-CLI hook survives force install and\nuninstall.\n\nAlso from review of this layer:\n- add the missing test seam for doctor's probe-error branch\n  (SetHooksDirProbeErrorForTesting) and pin that checkGlobalTracking\n  prints GIT HOOK STATE UNVERIFIED without clearing the\n  global_setup_completed marker when the residency probe fails\n- refactor ValidateGlobalConfig into pure ValidateGlobalPatterns over\n  the loaded config plus a thin loading wrapper, and pass the loaded\n  config into UnnormalizableOrigins — doctor loaded the settings file\n  three times per run; it now loads once. exclude_paths_exact entries\n  are validated too (tilde-expansion only; they are not globs)\n- record the third-agent availability-gate contract on the User-Level\n  Hook Support checklist section (trail 968 finding 019fef03-2ad1)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\ned6cbc577\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\nd4a26822d\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/paths/entire_join_guard_test.go\n\n---\n4567246e5\nfix(hooks): never fail TurnStart/SubagentStart on unroutable runtime paths\n\nThree invisible-tracking fixes from review:\n\nTurnStart and SubagentStart propagated paths.ErrUnroutableRuntimePath\nfrom CapturePrePromptState/CapturePreTaskState straight out of the hook,\nexiting non-zero on every prompt in a globally tracked repo whose\ngit-side location cannot be resolved — violating the sentinel's own\n'never fail the user's operation' contract and contradicting turn-end,\nwhich already skips. Both handlers now mirror the turn-end pattern:\nWarn (pre-state capture skipped this turn) and continue, keeping\nstate.go's 'callers skip' contract true. Attribution safety when the\nbaseline is skipped: in the steady unroutable state turn-end skips\ncheckpoint capture entirely before attribution; only an asymmetric\ntransient failure reaches the nil-preState path, which is the\nlong-standing no-TurnStart behavior shared with exec-mode agents.\n\nEnsurePrimaryRef wrote five ✓ bootstrap notices unconditionally to\nos.Stderr, leaking into agent hook output (observed live). The writer\nis now threaded through (EnsurePrimaryRefTo/createOrphanMetadataRef);\nhook-context callers — MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup and EnsureSetupForHook's\nensureSetup — pass io.Discard, while interactive flows (enable, agent\nsetup) keep os.Stderr via the unchanged EnsurePrimaryRef/EnsureSetup\nentry points.\n\nTestNoDirectEntireJoins' allowlist was file-scoped; it now requires an\ninline '// entire-join-ok: <reason>' marker per call site, so a new\nbypass in an already-audited file is still flagged and deleting a\nmarker re-flags its site (mutation-verified).\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":8292},"formatted_output":"e0d5732cd feat(settings): add user-global settings tier with exclude lists\nceb99f9cc feat(hooks): consult the user-global tier at both hook gates\n42034a2ef feat(hooks): lazy invisible enable for globally tracked repos\n745526e59 fix(global): per-worktree invisible routing + route diagnostics through AbsPath (namespacing portion; diagnostics routing lands in the agent-hooks split, migration scoping in the writer split)\n94ae1fcef feat(enable): global tracking writer — enable/disable --global, ask-once wizard, runtime-data migration\n269289137 fix(global): scope the enable-time runtime-data migration to the current worktree's namespace\n52d47fdee feat(global): user-level agent hooks — install/status/doctor + wrong-folder notice\ncb180a524 fix(global): per-worktree invisible routing + route diagnostics through AbsPath\n802db6efb test(global): derive enable --global flag-conflict coverage; pin redaction configuration under global mode\n6e752cf90 docs(hooks): correct the initHookLogging gate-ordering comment\nc7fb1f6ef fix(settings): trim whitespace in exclude patterns; document remote scope choice\nab7d9f6fc test(settings): pin leading-whitespace tilde pattern expansion\nbe759ce3b Merge feat/global-core fixes forward\n095d66150 Merge feat/global-invisible fixes forward\n98d75792d fix(global): context-aware wizard prompt; isolate git config in worktree test\na68aba05e Merge feat/global-writer fixes forward\nf8c7e9375 fix(global): context-aware removal prompt; user-scope installs skip permissions parse; type-aware flag-conflict test\n68958f183 fix(settings): fail-closed exclusion, symlink-robust path matching, gate tests\n6215560f4 Merge feat/global-core (fail-closed exclusion hardening) into feat/global-invisible\n1be819ab5 Merge feat/global-invisible forward (fail-closed exclusion hardening)\n87d4f1d7d Merge feat/global-writer forward (fail-closed exclusion hardening)\n03cd547fd docs(settings): state the GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract\n51e6787e8 Merge feat/global-invisible forward (GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract)\n142d66329 Merge feat/global-writer forward (GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract)\n1ec6d51f8 feat(doctor): validate global-tracking settings — surface what dead hook logs cannot\nb46a09013 fix(paths,strategy): invisible routing and lazy setup fail toward invisibility\n36e227d10 chore(paths): comment corrections, layout contract export, invariant tests\nb2dd7332a Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\na2206e00e refactor(setup): consume the exported invisible-layout contract\n1ef56897f Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n8da96a889 feat(doctor): explain worktree-resident hooksPath instead of clearing the marker\n84ae1681d fix(lifecycle): unroutable runtime path skips the turn-end capture instead of failing the hook\nfca583b52 Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n7dd63f421 Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\nc38fac9ad chore(doctor): align hooksPath explanation with sibling header style\nde39598ae fix(global): repo-level takeover runs everywhere a settings file is born\nfbde176f3 test(global): pin the writer layer's promises; comment corrections\n332d61e79 Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\nb90de4e82 refactor(settings): nil-safe global accessors, locked user-settings writes, shared pattern check\ne6d4c49a7 fix(global): review fold-ins — consent-race recheck, capped migration warns, actionable gitignore warn\na26b7ac2d Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n22041897c fix(global): verb-scoped hook recognition, atomic writes, and lossless merges for agent settings\n82f6c62c3 fix(global): honest diagnostics — error-aware hook checks, per-repo status truth, doctor probe handling\nf80ac2284 docs(global): correct stale and overbroad comments on the global-tracking surfaces\n2ac3ec1d8 fix(global): residual user-scope writer issues — dangling symlinks, file modes, gemini recognition/completeness, honest repair reporting\n190783286 fix(global): deliver the inactive SessionStart notice through the agent's hook-response channel\ne707f826f docs(global): correct the gemini user-hook no-double-fire mechanism\n5f9f010a4 feat(settings): add exclude_paths_exact and polish the global gate API\nac70fd121 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n4567246e5 fix(hooks): never fail TurnStart/SubagentStart on unroutable runtime paths\nd4a26822d Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\ned6cbc577 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n8da187adf fix(agents): verb-scope repo-level hook recognition for the remaining agents\n182372f73 perf(settings): pin the global gate's no-fork fast path\n4f33d9f48 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n9ae3a994c Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n5dc4f6435 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n39a39ce1b fix(status): render every in-repo inactive reason on the global tracking line\n3f45f68db fix(settings): lock the user-global settings writers at the layer that introduces them\n1d3f451ad Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n9d0531062 fix(global): route diagnostics through AbsPath; settings writers observe their own writes\nd0374492c fix(global): doctor bundle degrades instead of aborting on an unroutable logs path\ne9d2fbfcc fix(global): doctor logs / trace name the routing failure instead of \"not a git repository\"\na6bc064c0 feat(settings): trust schema, RepoTrustIdentity, and the checkpoint egress predicate\n8d65b8273 feat(strategy): hold checkpoint egress for untrusted globally-enrolled repos; y/n/A trust prompt at interactive pushes\nf5fd5b1b3 feat(cli): entire trust command, detection warn, and trust surfaces across status/doctor/session-start\n6b62828c4 docs+test(global): trust-gate docs section and end-to-end held/trusted push coverage\n7ae8dd485 test(global): apply test audit — drop redundant pins, strengthen revoke no-op, cover prompt-error and hand-edit tolerance\nc9e788c67 fix(global): apply toolkit review round — pushurl-aware trust identity, wizard warn ack, inactive-tier refusal, poisoned-path resilience\nd91eeeef7 test(global): enforce the Tests and Comments policy\nc82ffe01f test(global): reduce test volume to the integration-anchored core; strip rationale comments\n0c3bb8158 fix(global): close origin-exclusion fail-open gaps\n3b66859ff fix(gitremote): preserve context cancellation through the repo-ness probe\n04f7bf491 fix(global): guard runtime-data migration against live writers and divergent leftovers\n92b05e182 fix(settings): fail closed on malformed exclude_origins without an origin (D gate shape)\nfd384895c test(global): reduce test volume toward the integration-anchored core\n499e87670 fix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n2b35db349 fix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\ncd7dd8a7b fix(jsonutil): apply the temp file's mode via fd-based chmod before close\n549d1f0c1 fix(gitremote): never swallow a cancellation into \"no origin configured\"\ndad799740 fix(global): fsync the migration copy before removing its source\n03b9b2dec fix(paths): propagate context cancellation through the routing probe\n6e4840470 fix(paths): a cached routing error must not mask the caller's cancellation\n9daa4e6c0 fix(global): bare 'entire' respects the global tier; /.git origins normalize\n7aaeceb70 test(settings): pin Windows drive-letter absolutes through the exclude guard\nd676f4614 fix(global): serialize hook install/remove; harden the bare-entire and exclude guards\nf4423a32c fix(strategy): serialize hook install/remove across processes (B shape)\n98bee6472 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/global-core\n0bffa4822 Merge branch 'feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n400a52283 Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n1a1c5a27e Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n922f4ec57 Merge branch 'feat/global-agent-hooks' into feat/global-trust\n0b22946b6 test(strategy): make the install-lock regression test actually catch the race\n1856d4829 fix(global): don't remove the routed tree if a session activates mid-migration\n56182b440 perf(jsonutil): stop the symlink walk at a self-referential link\n717dc8e65 fix(jsonutil): name both paths when a symlinked write fails\ndadaf9cf2 docs: resolve leftover CLAUDE.md conflict markers from the D merge\nd93594059 Merge origin/main into feat/global-core\na8aa5b281 fix(global): preserve explicit activation intent\nd91860ce9 Merge feat/global-core into feat/global-invisible\n82a3d08da fix(strategy): document best-effort setup skip\n730a1763a Merge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n1152c3dd3 Merge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n1e753a46f Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n922f9f18e fix(global): require Claude subagent stop user hook\ne22e39f2f Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n3e76fbba9 fix(settings): enforce trusted activation intent\n5e89a4bfe Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\ncd861285d fix(paths): keep tracked local activation invisible\n31e7cd5c7 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n593d526a9 fix(global): avoid overwriting live migration data\n8bd406e5b Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n2ba044d30 fix(claude): verify every user lifecycle hook\n92f40315b fix(paths): preserve activation under cancellation\n5a85aed6f fix(global): serialize hooks with runtime migration\n875b2d746 fix(hooks): log inactive response failures\nd749591c6 merge: propagate global enable stack fixes\n5144d12d4 (origin/feat/global-core, feat/global-core) perf(settings): fold exclusion paths once\n66e2c6e70 merge: propagate exclusion matching fix\n5e61e13bc merge: propagate global enable fixes\neec513577 merge: propagate global enable fixes\nf099212da merge: propagate global enable fixes\n646585363 (origin/feat/global-invisible, feat/global-invisible) fix(paths): stop invisible fallbacks on cancellation\nd1493af16 Merge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n0201d7f7e (origin/feat/global-agent-hooks, feat/global-agent-hooks) Merge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\nfd60aa12e Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\na92031b1b (origin/feat/global-writer, feat/global-writer) fix: harden global runtime takeover\n3d1874fe3 merge: consolidate global enable stack\nbca00205a (HEAD -> fix/global-takeover-migration, origin/feat/global-trust, feat/global-trust) merge: integrate current main into global enable\n3d1874fe3\nmerge: consolidate global enable stack\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0TPDDEDFB3YH22Y1Q7BYMBD\n\n---\na92031b1b\nfix: harden global runtime takeover\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0TMAK37EEM2MHT8XMYGK0AF\n\n---\nfd60aa12e\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\n---\n0201d7f7e\nMerge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n---\nd1493af16\nMerge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n\n---\n646585363\nfix(paths): stop invisible fallbacks on cancellation\n\n---\nf099212da\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\neec513577\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\n5e61e13bc\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\n\n---\n66e2c6e70\nmerge: propagate exclusion matching fix\n\n---\n5144d12d4\nperf(settings): fold exclusion paths once\n\n---\nd749591c6\nmerge: propagate global enable stack fixes\n\n---\n875b2d746\nfix(hooks): log inactive response failures\n\n---\n5a85aed6f\nfix(global): serialize hooks with runtime migration\n\n---\n92f40315b\nfix(paths): preserve activation under cancellation\n\n---\n2ba044d30\nfix(claude): verify every user lifecycle hook\n\n---\n8bd406e5b\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n---\n593d526a9\nfix(global): avoid overwriting live migration data\n\n---\n31e7cd5c7\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n---\ncd861285d\nfix(paths): keep tracked local activation invisible\n\n---\ne22e39f2f\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\nCarry the Claude SubagentStop user-hook completeness repair into the final trust-gate branch.\n\n---\n922f9f18e\nfix(global): require Claude subagent stop user hook\n\nKeep user-level completeness aligned with repo-level freshness so a partial install is detected and repaired.\n\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0JSMPDC8WGT2616NAP2J95X\n\n---\n1e753a46f\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\n\nCarry explicit repo activation intent through checkpoint egress, trust commands, and status. Incidental settings continue through the global trust gate; malformed activation settings hold data locally.\n\n---\n1152c3dd3\nMerge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\nCarry explicit repo activation intent through status reasons and user-level hook coverage. Preserve the safer user-settings writer while integrating Claude Code SubagentStop support.\n\n---\n730a1763a\nMerge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\n\nCarry explicit activation-intent semantics through first-run setup, repo takeover, and user-global writes.\n\n---\n82a3d08da\nfix(strategy): document best-effort setup skip\n\n---\nd91860ce9\nMerge feat/global-core into feat/global-invisible\n\nPreserve explicit activation-intent semantics in invisible runtime routing and lazy hook setup.\n\n---\na8aa5b281\nfix(global): preserve explicit activation intent\n\n---\n1856d4829\nfix(global): don't remove the routed tree if a session activates mid-migration\n\nTrail 1014 finding on the TOCTOU window between the active-session check\nand the moves. The window is real and cannot be closed from this side:\nhook runtime-data writes (lifecycle's prompt.txt and full.jsonl) take no\nlock, so a migration-side lock would only serialize concurrent enables.\nWhat CAN be narrowed is the damage — re-check after the moves and skip\ndirectory removal, the one remaining destructive step, which is what\nturns a live hook's write into ENOENT. Leftovers cost only a later\nsweep: a non-empty routed dir re-triggers migration on the next enable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n922f4ec57\nMerge branch 'feat/global-agent-hooks' into feat/global-trust\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tCLAUDE.md\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go\n\n---\n1a1c5a27e\nMerge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/hooks_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/factoryaidroid/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go\n\n---\n400a52283\nMerge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/setup.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go\n\n---\n0bffa4822\nMerge branch 'feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks_test.go\n\n---\nd676f4614\nfix(global): serialize hook install/remove; harden the bare-entire and exclude guards\n\nTrail 1012 findings:\n\n- Concurrent first-install race (HIGH): global mode moves first-ever git\n  hook installation into hook processes that fire concurrently, and the\n  unsynchronized read→rename→write could rename a half-installed wrapper\n  over the user's hook backup — destroying the hook and leaving a\n  wrapper chaining to itself. InstallGitHook and RemoveGitHook now take\n  a cross-process flock in the git common dir (never the hooks dir,\n  which can be worktree-resident). Regression test mutation-verified:\n  fails on the unlocked code with the exact self-chain corruption.\n- Bare 'entire' no longer treats an UNUSABLE global config as \"tier says\n  no\": the gate reads the enabled bit itself — an unreadable settings\n  file gets a stderr warning instead of a wizard that would pin the repo\n  out of the tier, and a tier-enabled-but-excluded repo is not funneled\n  into repo-level setup either.\n- expandTilde accepts only filepath.IsAbs patterns: the leading-slash\n  allowance was redundant on Unix and fail-open on Windows, where the\n  MSYS spelling /c/code/** can never match a drive-rooted root.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n6e4840470\nfix(paths): a cached routing error must not mask the caller's cancellation\n\nTrail 1013 finding: the memo's hit path returned a cached\nErrUnroutableRuntimePath to callers arriving with an already-canceled\ncontext, misreporting their cancellation as a routing failure. A cached\nerror now yields the cancellation instead; a cached BASE is still served\n— the memo read needs no I/O, and teardown paths may resolve paths under\nan already-canceled context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n03b9b2dec\nfix(paths): propagate context cancellation through the routing probe\n\nTrail 1013 finding: a canceled context failing the git-common-dir probe\nwas wrapped as ErrUnroutableRuntimePath, turning a dying process's\ncancellation into the callers' silent skip; propagate the cancellation\ninstead (same fix as gitremote's repo-ness probe). Also never cache a\ncancellation-tainted result — the memo would otherwise poison every\nlater resolution in the process with the stale cancellation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\ndad799740\nfix(global): fsync the migration copy before removing its source\n\nTrail 1014 finding: copyFileThenRemove renamed and then deleted the\nsource without syncing the temp file, so a crash could surface the\nrename with the bytes still in cache — losing the file outright since\nthe source is already gone. Sync before close, matching WriteFileAtomic.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n2b35db349\nfix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n\nTrail 1016 findings: mirrors feat/global-core's 499e87670 into this\nbranch's copy of the gate (identical hunks for the landing merge), and\nadds two clarifying doc lines the same review asked after — ensureHook's\nshared snapshot cannot overcount (every call checks a distinct\nmatcher/command pair), and resolveWriteTarget keeps relative paths\nrelative (EvalSymlinks never absolutizes).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n499e87670\nfix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\n\nTrail 1016 finding: prefer Match over the ValidatePattern+MatchUnvalidated\npairing so the matching call itself can never run an assumed-valid pattern;\nthe ValidatePattern pass stays for the no-origin vet path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n92b05e182\nfix(settings): fail closed on malformed exclude_origins without an origin (D gate shape)\n\nMirrors feat/global-core's 0c3bb8158 into this branch's rewrite of the\ngate: computeGlobalModeStatus vets the exclude_origins list before the\norigin lookup, and matchesExcludeOrigin validates every pattern even\nwith an empty origin — this branch's version of the function supersedes\nthe base's at landing, so it must carry the same fail-closed behavior.\nText mirrors the base commit so the landing merge sees identical hunks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n04f7bf491\nfix(global): guard runtime-data migration against live writers and divergent leftovers\n\nTrail 1014 findings on maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData:\n\n- A destination file that already exists is dropped from the source only\n  when its content is identical; a divergent or uncomparable pair now\n  counts as failed — into the summary's 'left in <source>' bucket — where\n  a blind skip previously stranded the source under .git silently and\n  forever.\n- Migration defers (with a printed re-run hint) when a session is ACTIVE\n  in this worktree: a hook process may be mid-write under the routed dir,\n  where a rename strands its in-flight file and the EXDEV copy fallback\n  can snapshot a half-written one. Idle sessions and other worktrees'\n  sessions don't defer. The non-empty routed dir re-triggers migration on\n  the next enable, which is the documented recovery point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n0c3bb8158\nfix(global): close origin-exclusion fail-open gaps\n\nReview findings on trail 1012:\n\n- splitOwnerRepo sheds trailing slashes and any-case \".git\", so a stored\n  origin like https://github.com/acme/widgets/ normalizes to\n  github.com/acme/widgets instead of a form no exclude pattern matches\n  (fail-open), and every ParseURL caller stops seeing \"widgets/\" repos.\n- matchesExcludeOrigin validates every pattern even without an origin, and\n  GlobalModeActive vets the list before the origin lookup, so a malformed\n  exclude_origins entry fails closed identically whether or not the repo\n  has an origin.\n- GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet reports a blank 'url =' value as found=true with\n  the empty value (the gate fails closed on it) and errors on a non-repo\n  dir instead of misreading git's scope-fallback exit 1 as \"no origin\n  configured\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nc82ffe01f\ntest(global): reduce test volume to the integration-anchored core; strip rationale comments\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nc9e788c67\nfix(global): apply toolkit review round — pushurl-aware trust identity, wizard warn ack, inactive-tier refusal, poisoned-path resilience\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\nf5fd5b1b3\nfeat(cli): entire trust command, detection warn, and trust surfaces across status/doctor/session-start\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M08T1GNCGPYG9T71HPB70R9S\n\n---\n8d65b8273\nfeat(strategy): hold checkpoint egress for untrusted globally-enrolled repos; y/n/A trust prompt at interactive pushes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\na6bc064c0\nfeat(settings): trust schema, RepoTrustIdentity, and the checkpoint egress predicate\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n9d0531062\nfix(global): route diagnostics through AbsPath; settings writers observe their own writes\n\nFixes both open trail findings on this layer:\n\n- 019ff8ab-9a2: doctor bundle/logs/trace built log paths as\n  filepath.Join(repoRoot, logging.LogsDir), silently producing empty\n  diagnostics for globally tracked repos (addDirToZip skips a missing\n  dir without error; doctor logs reports \"No log file\"). All three now\n  resolve through paths.AbsPath, with one routed-logs test per command.\n  Ported verbatim from the agent-hooks layer upstack so the merge-up\n  stays content-identical.\n\n- 019ff8ab-97d: the invisibleCache comment claimed the enable/disable\n  layers already call ClearInvisibleRuntimeCache, but nothing at this\n  layer did: `entire enable` latches the pre-write routing decision\n  (logging.Init resolves .entire/logs before settings.json exists) for\n  the rest of the process. saveRaw/saveToFile now clear the cache after\n  every write (ported from the writer layer upstack, which keeps its\n  identical hunks), and the comment now states what holds at this layer.\n  TestRepoSettingsWrites_ClearInvisibleRoutingCache pins the contract;\n  the upstack copy in global_save_test.go supersedes it on merge.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n3f45f68db\nfix(settings): lock the user-global settings writers at the layer that introduces them\n\nAll three writers (enable --global, disable --global, the wizard prompt) did\nan unlocked load-modify-save of ~/.config/entire/settings.json; the wizard's\npre-persist re-check only narrowed its race. ModifyUserSettings now runs the\ncycle under the same flock pattern used for clone preferences, the wizard's\nsupersede check moves inside the locked callback, and SaveUserSettings\ndelegates so no unlocked write path remains. The upstack layer carries the\nsame shape; this puts the lock in the PR where the writers are born so the\nstack never merges an unlocked window onto main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n5dc4f6435\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\n9ae3a994c\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\n4f33d9f48\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\n\n---\n182372f73\nperf(settings): pin the global gate's no-fork fast path\n\nReview of the stack tip caught the memoized gate variant resolving\npaths.WorktreeRoot — a git rev-parse subprocess fork — before the cheap\nnil/disabled settings check, taxing every hook invocation in every repo\nwithout repo-level setup even when the global tier is unconfigured (the\nmachine-wide common case). This layer's GlobalModeActive already checks\nsettings first; make that ordering a stated invariant (doc comment),\nroute the resolution through a worktreeRootFn seam, and add a test that\nfails if the unconfigured/disabled path ever resolves the root. The\nmemoized variants upstack are reordered to satisfy the same test as the\nstack re-merges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\n8da187adf\nfix(agents): verb-scope repo-level hook recognition for the remaining agents\n\nPropagate the verb-scoped recognizer this round shipped for claude-code\nand gemini at user scope to the four agents that still matched managed\nhooks by the bare 'entire ' prefix at repo scope: codex, cursor,\ncopilot-cli, and factoryai-droid. A user-authored hook that merely\ninvokes the entire CLI (e.g. 'entire status --json > /tmp/s.json') was\nrecognized as ours and destroyed on uninstall or force reinstall. Every\nprefix is now scoped to '... hooks ', and every legacy local-dev form an\nolder installer wrote (unquoted then quoted rev-parse go-run) is\nretained verb-scoped. opencode and pi recognize their generated file by\na whole-file marker, not command prefixes — unchanged. Per-agent tests\npin that a user-authored entire-CLI hook survives force install and\nuninstall.\n\nAlso from review of this layer:\n- add the missing test seam for doctor's probe-error branch\n  (SetHooksDirProbeErrorForTesting) and pin that checkGlobalTracking\n  prints GIT HOOK STATE UNVERIFIED without clearing the\n  global_setup_completed marker when the residency probe fails\n- refactor ValidateGlobalConfig into pure ValidateGlobalPatterns over\n  the loaded config plus a thin loading wrapper, and pass the loaded\n  config into UnnormalizableOrigins — doctor loaded the settings file\n  three times per run; it now loads once. exclude_paths_exact entries\n  are validated too (tilde-expansion only; they are not globs)\n- record the third-agent availability-gate contract on the User-Level\n  Hook Support checklist section (trail 968 finding 019fef03-2ad1)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---\ned6cbc577\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\n\n---\nd4a26822d\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tcmd/entire/cli/paths/entire_join_guard_test.go\n\n---\n4567246e5\nfix(hooks): never fail TurnStart/SubagentStart on unroutable runtime paths\n\nThree invisible-tracking fixes from review:\n\nTurnStart and SubagentStart propagated paths.ErrUnroutableRuntimePath\nfrom CapturePrePromptState/CapturePreTaskState straight out of the hook,\nexiting non-zero on every prompt in a globally tracked repo whose\ngit-side location cannot be resolved — violating the sentinel's own\n'never fail the user's operation' contract and contradicting turn-end,\nwhich already skips. Both handlers now mirror the turn-end pattern:\nWarn (pre-state capture skipped this turn) and continue, keeping\nstate.go's 'callers skip' contract true. Attribution safety when the\nbaseline is skipped: in the steady unroutable state turn-end skips\ncheckpoint capture entirely before attribution; only an asymmetric\ntransient failure reaches the nil-preState path, which is the\nlong-standing no-TurnStart behavior shared with exec-mode agents.\n\nEnsurePrimaryRef wrote five ✓ bootstrap notices unconditionally to\nos.Stderr, leaking into agent hook output (observed live). The writer\nis now threaded through (EnsurePrimaryRefTo/createOrphanMetadataRef);\nhook-context callers — MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup and EnsureSetupForHook's\nensureSetup — pass io.Discard, while interactive flows (enable, agent\nsetup) keep os.Stderr via the unchanged EnsurePrimaryRef/EnsureSetup\nentry points.\n\nTestNoDirectEntireJoins' allowlist was file-scoped; it now requires an\ninline '// entire-join-ok: <reason>' marker per call site, so a new\nbypass in an already-audited file is still flagged and deleting a\nmarker re-flags its site (mutation-verified).\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1787608542837,"completed_at_ms":1787608542837}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:55:43.064Z","ordinal":9835,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a035c5-af58-70c0-a845-4805f99cf4ac","call_id":"call_9VmZEezhGko03MAVBOJibnmY","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"9de5b2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008292,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":7412,\"output\":\"e0d5732cd feat(settings): add user-global settings tier with exclude lists\\nceb99f9cc feat(hooks): consult the user-global tier at both hook gates\\n42034a2ef feat(hooks): lazy invisible enable for globally tracked repos\\n745526e59 fix(global): per-worktree invisible routing + route diagnostics through AbsPath (namespacing portion; diagnostics routing lands in the agent-hooks split, migration scoping in the writer split)\\n94ae1fcef feat(enable): global tracking writer — enable/disable --global, ask-once wizard, runtime-data migration\\n269289137 fix(global): scope the enable-time runtime-data migration to the current worktree's namespace\\n52d47fdee feat(global): user-level agent hooks — install/status/doctor + wrong-folder notice\\ncb180a524 fix(global): per-worktree invisible routing + route diagnostics through AbsPath\\n802db6efb test(global): derive enable --global flag-conflict coverage; pin redaction configuration under global mode\\n6e752cf90 docs(hooks): correct the initHookLogging gate-ordering comment\\nc7fb1f6ef fix(settings): trim whitespace in exclude patterns; document remote scope choice\\nab7d9f6fc test(settings): pin leading-whitespace tilde pattern expansion\\nbe759ce3b Merge feat/global-core fixes forward\\n095d66150 Merge feat/global-invisible fixes forward\\n98d75792d fix(global): context-aware wizard prompt; isolate git config in worktree test\\na68aba05e Merge feat/global-writer fixes forward\\nf8c7e9375 fix(global): context-aware removal prompt; user-scope installs skip permissions parse; type-aware flag-conflict test\\n68958f183 fix(settings): fail-closed exclusion, symlink-robust path matching, gate tests\\n6215560f4 Merge feat/global-core (fail-closed exclusion hardening) into feat/global-invisible\\n1be819ab5 Merge feat/global-invisible forward (fail-closed exclusion hardening)\\n87d4f1d7d Merge feat/global-writer forward (fail-closed exclusion hardening)\\n03cd547fd docs(settings): state the GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract\\n51e6787e8 Merge feat/global-invisible forward (GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract)\\n142d66329 Merge feat/global-writer forward (GloballyEnabled drift-clearing contract)\\n1ec6d51f8 feat(doctor): validate global-tracking settings — surface what dead hook logs cannot\\nb46a09013 fix(paths,strategy): invisible routing and lazy setup fail toward invisibility\\n36e227d10 chore(paths): comment corrections, layout contract export, invariant tests\\nb2dd7332a Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\na2206e00e refactor(setup): consume the exported invisible-layout contract\\n1ef56897f Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n8da96a889 feat(doctor): explain worktree-resident hooksPath instead of clearing the marker\\n84ae1681d fix(lifecycle): unroutable runtime path skips the turn-end capture instead of failing the hook\\nfca583b52 Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\n7dd63f421 Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\nc38fac9ad chore(doctor): align hooksPath explanation with sibling header style\\nde39598ae fix(global): repo-level takeover runs everywhere a settings file is born\\nfbde176f3 test(global): pin the writer layer's promises; comment corrections\\n332d61e79 Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\nb90de4e82 refactor(settings): nil-safe global accessors, locked user-settings writes, shared pattern check\\ne6d4c49a7 fix(global): review fold-ins — consent-race recheck, capped migration warns, actionable gitignore warn\\na26b7ac2d Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n22041897c fix(global): verb-scoped hook recognition, atomic writes, and lossless merges for agent settings\\n82f6c62c3 fix(global): honest diagnostics — error-aware hook checks, per-repo status truth, doctor probe handling\\nf80ac2284 docs(global): correct stale and overbroad comments on the global-tracking surfaces\\n2ac3ec1d8 fix(global): residual user-scope writer issues — dangling symlinks, file modes, gemini recognition/completeness, honest repair reporting\\n190783286 fix(global): deliver the inactive SessionStart notice through the agent's hook-response channel\\ne707f826f docs(global): correct the gemini user-hook no-double-fire mechanism\\n5f9f010a4 feat(settings): add exclude_paths_exact and polish the global gate API\\nac70fd121 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\\n4567246e5 fix(hooks): never fail TurnStart/SubagentStart on unroutable runtime paths\\nd4a26822d Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\ned6cbc577 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n8da187adf fix(agents): verb-scope repo-level hook recognition for the remaining agents\\n182372f73 perf(settings): pin the global gate's no-fork fast path\\n4f33d9f48 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\\n9ae3a994c Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\n5dc4f6435 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n39a39ce1b fix(status): render every in-repo inactive reason on the global tracking line\\n3f45f68db fix(settings): lock the user-global settings writers at the layer that introduces them\\n1d3f451ad Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n9d0531062 fix(global): route diagnostics through AbsPath; settings writers observe their own writes\\nd0374492c fix(global): doctor bundle degrades instead of aborting on an unroutable logs path\\ne9d2fbfcc fix(global): doctor logs / trace name the routing failure instead of \\\"not a git repository\\\"\\na6bc064c0 feat(settings): trust schema, RepoTrustIdentity, and the checkpoint egress predicate\\n8d65b8273 feat(strategy): hold checkpoint egress for untrusted globally-enrolled repos; y/n/A trust prompt at interactive pushes\\nf5fd5b1b3 feat(cli): entire trust command, detection warn, and trust surfaces across status/doctor/session-start\\n6b62828c4 docs+test(global): trust-gate docs section and end-to-end held/trusted push coverage\\n7ae8dd485 test(global): apply test audit — drop redundant pins, strengthen revoke no-op, cover prompt-error and hand-edit tolerance\\nc9e788c67 fix(global): apply toolkit review round — pushurl-aware trust identity, wizard warn ack, inactive-tier refusal, poisoned-path resilience\\nd91eeeef7 test(global): enforce the Tests and Comments policy\\nc82ffe01f test(global): reduce test volume to the integration-anchored core; strip rationale comments\\n0c3bb8158 fix(global): close origin-exclusion fail-open gaps\\n3b66859ff fix(gitremote): preserve context cancellation through the repo-ness probe\\n04f7bf491 fix(global): guard runtime-data migration against live writers and divergent leftovers\\n92b05e182 fix(settings): fail closed on malformed exclude_origins without an origin (D gate shape)\\nfd384895c test(global): reduce test volume toward the integration-anchored core\\n499e87670 fix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\\n2b35db349 fix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\\ncd7dd8a7b fix(jsonutil): apply the temp file's mode via fd-based chmod before close\\n549d1f0c1 fix(gitremote): never swallow a cancellation into \\\"no origin configured\\\"\\ndad799740 fix(global): fsync the migration copy before removing its source\\n03b9b2dec fix(paths): propagate context cancellation through the routing probe\\n6e4840470 fix(paths): a cached routing error must not mask the caller's cancellation\\n9daa4e6c0 fix(global): bare 'entire' respects the global tier; /.git origins normalize\\n7aaeceb70 test(settings): pin Windows drive-letter absolutes through the exclude guard\\nd676f4614 fix(global): serialize hook install/remove; harden the bare-entire and exclude guards\\nf4423a32c fix(strategy): serialize hook install/remove across processes (B shape)\\n98bee6472 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/main' into feat/global-core\\n0bffa4822 Merge branch 'feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\\n400a52283 Merge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\n1a1c5a27e Merge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n922f4ec57 Merge branch 'feat/global-agent-hooks' into feat/global-trust\\n0b22946b6 test(strategy): make the install-lock regression test actually catch the race\\n1856d4829 fix(global): don't remove the routed tree if a session activates mid-migration\\n56182b440 perf(jsonutil): stop the symlink walk at a self-referential link\\n717dc8e65 fix(jsonutil): name both paths when a symlinked write fails\\ndadaf9cf2 docs: resolve leftover CLAUDE.md conflict markers from the D merge\\nd93594059 Merge origin/main into feat/global-core\\na8aa5b281 fix(global): preserve explicit activation intent\\nd91860ce9 Merge feat/global-core into feat/global-invisible\\n82a3d08da fix(strategy): document best-effort setup skip\\n730a1763a Merge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\\n1152c3dd3 Merge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n1e753a46f Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\\n922f9f18e fix(global): require Claude subagent stop user hook\\ne22e39f2f Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\\n3e76fbba9 fix(settings): enforce trusted activation intent\\n5e89a4bfe Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\\ncd861285d fix(paths): keep tracked local activation invisible\\n31e7cd5c7 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\n593d526a9 fix(global): avoid overwriting live migration data\\n8bd406e5b Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n2ba044d30 fix(claude): verify every user lifecycle hook\\n92f40315b fix(paths): preserve activation under cancellation\\n5a85aed6f fix(global): serialize hooks with runtime migration\\n875b2d746 fix(hooks): log inactive response failures\\nd749591c6 merge: propagate global enable stack fixes\\n5144d12d4 (origin/feat/global-core, feat/global-core) perf(settings): fold exclusion paths once\\n66e2c6e70 merge: propagate exclusion matching fix\\n5e61e13bc merge: propagate global enable fixes\\neec513577 merge: propagate global enable fixes\\nf099212da merge: propagate global enable fixes\\n646585363 (origin/feat/global-invisible, feat/global-invisible) fix(paths): stop invisible fallbacks on cancellation\\nd1493af16 Merge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\\n0201d7f7e (origin/feat/global-agent-hooks, feat/global-agent-hooks) Merge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\\nfd60aa12e Merge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\\na92031b1b (origin/feat/global-writer, feat/global-writer) fix: harden global runtime takeover\\n3d1874fe3 merge: consolidate global enable stack\\nbca00205a (HEAD -> fix/global-takeover-migration, origin/feat/global-trust, feat/global-trust) merge: integrate current main into global enable\\n3d1874fe3\\nmerge: consolidate global enable stack\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0TPDDEDFB3YH22Y1Q7BYMBD\\n\\n---\\na92031b1b\\nfix: harden global runtime takeover\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0TMAK37EEM2MHT8XMYGK0AF\\n\\n---\\nfd60aa12e\\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\\n\\n---\\n0201d7f7e\\nMerge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n\\n---\\nd1493af16\\nMerge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\\n\\n---\\n646585363\\nfix(paths): stop invisible fallbacks on cancellation\\n\\n---\\nf099212da\\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\\n\\n---\\neec513577\\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\\n\\n---\\n5e61e13bc\\nmerge: propagate global enable fixes\\n\\n---\\n66e2c6e70\\nmerge: propagate exclusion matching fix\\n\\n---\\n5144d12d4\\nperf(settings): fold exclusion paths once\\n\\n---\\nd749591c6\\nmerge: propagate global enable stack fixes\\n\\n---\\n875b2d746\\nfix(hooks): log inactive response failures\\n\\n---\\n5a85aed6f\\nfix(global): serialize hooks with runtime migration\\n\\n---\\n92f40315b\\nfix(paths): preserve activation under cancellation\\n\\n---\\n2ba044d30\\nfix(claude): verify every user lifecycle hook\\n\\n---\\n8bd406e5b\\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n\\n---\\n593d526a9\\nfix(global): avoid overwriting live migration data\\n\\n---\\n31e7cd5c7\\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\n\\n---\\ncd861285d\\nfix(paths): keep tracked local activation invisible\\n\\n---\\ne22e39f2f\\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\\n\\nCarry the Claude SubagentStop user-hook completeness repair into the final trust-gate branch.\\n\\n---\\n922f9f18e\\nfix(global): require Claude subagent stop user hook\\n\\nKeep user-level completeness aligned with repo-level freshness so a partial install is detected and repaired.\\n\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M0JSMPDC8WGT2616NAP2J95X\\n\\n---\\n1e753a46f\\nMerge feat/global-agent-hooks into feat/global-trust\\n\\nCarry explicit repo activation intent through checkpoint egress, trust commands, and status. Incidental settings continue through the global trust gate; malformed activation settings hold data locally.\\n\\n---\\n1152c3dd3\\nMerge feat/global-writer into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n\\nCarry explicit repo activation intent through status reasons and user-level hook coverage. Preserve the safer user-settings writer while integrating Claude Code SubagentStop support.\\n\\n---\\n730a1763a\\nMerge feat/global-invisible into feat/global-writer\\n\\nCarry explicit activation-intent semantics through first-run setup, repo takeover, and user-global writes.\\n\\n---\\n82a3d08da\\nfix(strategy): document best-effort setup skip\\n\\n---\\nd91860ce9\\nMerge feat/global-core into feat/global-invisible\\n\\nPreserve explicit activation-intent semantics in invisible runtime routing and lazy hook setup.\\n\\n---\\na8aa5b281\\nfix(global): preserve explicit activation intent\\n\\n---\\n1856d4829\\nfix(global): don't remove the routed tree if a session activates mid-migration\\n\\nTrail 1014 finding on the TOCTOU window between the active-session check\\nand the moves. The window is real and cannot be closed from this side:\\nhook runtime-data writes (lifecycle's prompt.txt and full.jsonl) take no\\nlock, so a migration-side lock would only serialize concurrent enables.\\nWhat CAN be narrowed is the damage — re-check after the moves and skip\\ndirectory removal, the one remaining destructive step, which is what\\nturns a live hook's write into ENOENT. Leftovers cost only a later\\nsweep: a non-empty routed dir re-triggers migration on the next enable.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n922f4ec57\\nMerge branch 'feat/global-agent-hooks' into feat/global-trust\\n\\n# Conflicts:\\n#\\tCLAUDE.md\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go\\n\\n---\\n1a1c5a27e\\nMerge branch 'feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n\\n# Conflicts:\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/hooks.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/hooks.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/hooks_test.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/factoryaidroid/hooks.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go\\n\\n---\\n400a52283\\nMerge branch 'feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\n\\n# Conflicts:\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/setup.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go\\n\\n---\\n0bffa4822\\nMerge branch 'feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\\n\\n# Conflicts:\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks_test.go\\n\\n---\\nd676f4614\\nfix(global): serialize hook install/remove; harden the bare-entire and exclude guards\\n\\nTrail 1012 findings:\\n\\n- Concurrent first-install race (HIGH): global mode moves first-ever git\\n  hook installation into hook processes that fire concurrently, and the\\n  unsynchronized read→rename→write could rename a half-installed wrapper\\n  over the user's hook backup — destroying the hook and leaving a\\n  wrapper chaining to itself. InstallGitHook and RemoveGitHook now take\\n  a cross-process flock in the git common dir (never the hooks dir,\\n  which can be worktree-resident). Regression test mutation-verified:\\n  fails on the unlocked code with the exact self-chain corruption.\\n- Bare 'entire' no longer treats an UNUSABLE global config as \\\"tier says\\n  no\\\": the gate reads the enabled bit itself — an unreadable settings\\n  file gets a stderr warning instead of a wizard that would pin the repo\\n  out of the tier, and a tier-enabled-but-excluded repo is not funneled\\n  into repo-level setup either.\\n- expandTilde accepts only filepath.IsAbs patterns: the leading-slash\\n  allowance was redundant on Unix and fail-open on Windows, where the\\n  MSYS spelling /c/code/** can never match a drive-rooted root.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n6e4840470\\nfix(paths): a cached routing error must not mask the caller's cancellation\\n\\nTrail 1013 finding: the memo's hit path returned a cached\\nErrUnroutableRuntimePath to callers arriving with an already-canceled\\ncontext, misreporting their cancellation as a routing failure. A cached\\nerror now yields the cancellation instead; a cached BASE is still served\\n— the memo read needs no I/O, and teardown paths may resolve paths under\\nan already-canceled context.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n03b9b2dec\\nfix(paths): propagate context cancellation through the routing probe\\n\\nTrail 1013 finding: a canceled context failing the git-common-dir probe\\nwas wrapped as ErrUnroutableRuntimePath, turning a dying process's\\ncancellation into the callers' silent skip; propagate the cancellation\\ninstead (same fix as gitremote's repo-ness probe). Also never cache a\\ncancellation-tainted result — the memo would otherwise poison every\\nlater resolution in the process with the stale cancellation.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\ndad799740\\nfix(global): fsync the migration copy before removing its source\\n\\nTrail 1014 finding: copyFileThenRemove renamed and then deleted the\\nsource without syncing the temp file, so a crash could surface the\\nrename with the bytes still in cache — losing the file outright since\\nthe source is already gone. Sync before close, matching WriteFileAtomic.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n2b35db349\\nfix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\\n\\nTrail 1016 findings: mirrors feat/global-core's 499e87670 into this\\nbranch's copy of the gate (identical hunks for the landing merge), and\\nadds two clarifying doc lines the same review asked after — ensureHook's\\nshared snapshot cannot overcount (every call checks a distinct\\nmatcher/command pair), and resolveWriteTarget keeps relative paths\\nrelative (EvalSymlinks never absolutizes).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n499e87670\\nfix(settings): match exclude_origins with the validating doublestar.Match\\n\\nTrail 1016 finding: prefer Match over the ValidatePattern+MatchUnvalidated\\npairing so the matching call itself can never run an assumed-valid pattern;\\nthe ValidatePattern pass stays for the no-origin vet path.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n92b05e182\\nfix(settings): fail closed on malformed exclude_origins without an origin (D gate shape)\\n\\nMirrors feat/global-core's 0c3bb8158 into this branch's rewrite of the\\ngate: computeGlobalModeStatus vets the exclude_origins list before the\\norigin lookup, and matchesExcludeOrigin validates every pattern even\\nwith an empty origin — this branch's version of the function supersedes\\nthe base's at landing, so it must carry the same fail-closed behavior.\\nText mirrors the base commit so the landing merge sees identical hunks.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n04f7bf491\\nfix(global): guard runtime-data migration against live writers and divergent leftovers\\n\\nTrail 1014 findings on maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData:\\n\\n- A destination file that already exists is dropped from the source only\\n  when its content is identical; a divergent or uncomparable pair now\\n  counts as failed — into the summary's 'left in <source>' bucket — where\\n  a blind skip previously stranded the source under .git silently and\\n  forever.\\n- Migration defers (with a printed re-run hint) when a session is ACTIVE\\n  in this worktree: a hook process may be mid-write under the routed dir,\\n  where a rename strands its in-flight file and the EXDEV copy fallback\\n  can snapshot a half-written one. Idle sessions and other worktrees'\\n  sessions don't defer. The non-empty routed dir re-triggers migration on\\n  the next enable, which is the documented recovery point.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n0c3bb8158\\nfix(global): close origin-exclusion fail-open gaps\\n\\nReview findings on trail 1012:\\n\\n- splitOwnerRepo sheds trailing slashes and any-case \\\".git\\\", so a stored\\n  origin like https://github.com/acme/widgets/ normalizes to\\n  github.com/acme/widgets instead of a form no exclude pattern matches\\n  (fail-open), and every ParseURL caller stops seeing \\\"widgets/\\\" repos.\\n- matchesExcludeOrigin validates every pattern even without an origin, and\\n  GlobalModeActive vets the list before the origin lookup, so a malformed\\n  exclude_origins entry fails closed identically whether or not the repo\\n  has an origin.\\n- GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet reports a blank 'url =' value as found=true with\\n  the empty value (the gate fails closed on it) and errors on a non-repo\\n  dir instead of misreading git's scope-fallback exit 1 as \\\"no origin\\n  configured\\\".\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\nc82ffe01f\\ntest(global): reduce test volume to the integration-anchored core; strip rationale comments\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\nc9e788c67\\nfix(global): apply toolkit review round — pushurl-aware trust identity, wizard warn ack, inactive-tier refusal, poisoned-path resilience\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\nf5fd5b1b3\\nfeat(cli): entire trust command, detection warn, and trust surfaces across status/doctor/session-start\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\nEntire-Checkpoint: 01M08T1GNCGPYG9T71HPB70R9S\\n\\n---\\n8d65b8273\\nfeat(strategy): hold checkpoint egress for untrusted globally-enrolled repos; y/n/A trust prompt at interactive pushes\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\na6bc064c0\\nfeat(settings): trust schema, RepoTrustIdentity, and the checkpoint egress predicate\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n9d0531062\\nfix(global): route diagnostics through AbsPath; settings writers observe their own writes\\n\\nFixes both open trail findings on this layer:\\n\\n- 019ff8ab-9a2: doctor bundle/logs/trace built log paths as\\n  filepath.Join(repoRoot, logging.LogsDir), silently producing empty\\n  diagnostics for globally tracked repos (addDirToZip skips a missing\\n  dir without error; doctor logs reports \\\"No log file\\\"). All three now\\n  resolve through paths.AbsPath, with one routed-logs test per command.\\n  Ported verbatim from the agent-hooks layer upstack so the merge-up\\n  stays content-identical.\\n\\n- 019ff8ab-97d: the invisibleCache comment claimed the enable/disable\\n  layers already call ClearInvisibleRuntimeCache, but nothing at this\\n  layer did: `entire enable` latches the pre-write routing decision\\n  (logging.Init resolves .entire/logs before settings.json exists) for\\n  the rest of the process. saveRaw/saveToFile now clear the cache after\\n  every write (ported from the writer layer upstack, which keeps its\\n  identical hunks), and the comment now states what holds at this layer.\\n  TestRepoSettingsWrites_ClearInvisibleRoutingCache pins the contract;\\n  the upstack copy in global_save_test.go supersedes it on merge.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n3f45f68db\\nfix(settings): lock the user-global settings writers at the layer that introduces them\\n\\nAll three writers (enable --global, disable --global, the wizard prompt) did\\nan unlocked load-modify-save of ~/.config/entire/settings.json; the wizard's\\npre-persist re-check only narrowed its race. ModifyUserSettings now runs the\\ncycle under the same flock pattern used for clone preferences, the wizard's\\nsupersede check moves inside the locked callback, and SaveUserSettings\\ndelegates so no unlocked write path remains. The upstack layer carries the\\nsame shape; this puts the lock in the PR where the writers are born so the\\nstack never merges an unlocked window onto main.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n5dc4f6435\\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n\\n# Conflicts:\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\\n\\n---\\n9ae3a994c\\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\n\\n# Conflicts:\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\\n\\n---\\n4f33d9f48\\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-core' into feat/global-invisible\\n\\n---\\n182372f73\\nperf(settings): pin the global gate's no-fork fast path\\n\\nReview of the stack tip caught the memoized gate variant resolving\\npaths.WorktreeRoot — a git rev-parse subprocess fork — before the cheap\\nnil/disabled settings check, taxing every hook invocation in every repo\\nwithout repo-level setup even when the global tier is unconfigured (the\\nmachine-wide common case). This layer's GlobalModeActive already checks\\nsettings first; make that ordering a stated invariant (doc comment),\\nroute the resolution through a worktreeRootFn seam, and add a test that\\nfails if the unconfigured/disabled path ever resolves the root. The\\nmemoized variants upstack are reordered to satisfy the same test as the\\nstack re-merges.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\n8da187adf\\nfix(agents): verb-scope repo-level hook recognition for the remaining agents\\n\\nPropagate the verb-scoped recognizer this round shipped for claude-code\\nand gemini at user scope to the four agents that still matched managed\\nhooks by the bare 'entire ' prefix at repo scope: codex, cursor,\\ncopilot-cli, and factoryai-droid. A user-authored hook that merely\\ninvokes the entire CLI (e.g. 'entire status --json > /tmp/s.json') was\\nrecognized as ours and destroyed on uninstall or force reinstall. Every\\nprefix is now scoped to '... hooks ', and every legacy local-dev form an\\nolder installer wrote (unquoted then quoted rev-parse go-run) is\\nretained verb-scoped. opencode and pi recognize their generated file by\\na whole-file marker, not command prefixes — unchanged. Per-agent tests\\npin that a user-authored entire-CLI hook survives force install and\\nuninstall.\\n\\nAlso from review of this layer:\\n- add the missing test seam for doctor's probe-error branch\\n  (SetHooksDirProbeErrorForTesting) and pin that checkGlobalTracking\\n  prints GIT HOOK STATE UNVERIFIED without clearing the\\n  global_setup_completed marker when the residency probe fails\\n- refactor ValidateGlobalConfig into pure ValidateGlobalPatterns over\\n  the loaded config plus a thin loading wrapper, and pass the loaded\\n  config into UnnormalizableOrigins — doctor loaded the settings file\\n  three times per run; it now loads once. exclude_paths_exact entries\\n  are validated too (tilde-expansion only; they are not globs)\\n- record the third-agent availability-gate contract on the User-Level\\n  Hook Support checklist section (trail 968 finding 019fef03-2ad1)\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---\\ned6cbc577\\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-writer' into feat/global-agent-hooks\\n\\n# Conflicts:\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go\\n\\n---\\nd4a26822d\\nMerge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/global-invisible' into feat/global-writer\\n\\n# Conflicts:\\n#\\tcmd/entire/cli/paths/entire_join_guard_test.go\\n\\n---\\n4567246e5\\nfix(hooks): never fail TurnStart/SubagentStart on unroutable runtime paths\\n\\nThree invisible-tracking fixes from review:\\n\\nTurnStart and SubagentStart propagated paths.ErrUnroutableRuntimePath\\nfrom CapturePrePromptState/CapturePreTaskState straight out of the hook,\\nexiting non-zero on every prompt in a globally tracked repo whose\\ngit-side location cannot be resolved — violating the sentinel's own\\n'never fail the user's operation' contract and contradicting turn-end,\\nwhich already skips. Both handlers now mirror the turn-end pattern:\\nWarn (pre-state capture skipped this turn) and continue, keeping\\nstate.go's 'callers skip' contract true. Attribution safety when the\\nbaseline is skipped: in the steady unroutable state turn-end skips\\ncheckpoint capture entirely before attribution; only an asymmetric\\ntransient failure reaches the nil-preState path, which is the\\nlong-standing no-TurnStart behavior shared with exec-mode agents.\\n\\nEnsurePrimaryRef wrote five ✓ bootstrap notices unconditionally to\\nos.Stderr, leaking into agent hook output (observed live). The writer\\nis now threaded through (EnsurePrimaryRefTo/createOrphanMetadataRef);\\nhook-context callers — MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup and EnsureSetupForHook's\\nensureSetup — pass io.Discard, while interactive flows (enable, agent\\nsetup) keep os.Stderr via the unchanged EnsurePrimaryRef/EnsureSetup\\nentry points.\\n\\nTestNoDirectEntireJoins' allowlist was file-scoped; it now requires an\\ninline '// entire-join-ok: <reason>' marker per call site, so a new\\nbypass in an already-audited file is still flagged and deleting a\\nmarker re-flags its site (mutation-verified).\\n\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787608543.064847}}}
