{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:56:41.717Z","ordinal":9905,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbe18b2d887d0b966dee7dd07274a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe safest decomposition follows state ownership: first define one policy snapshot, then make storage routing consume it, then update hooks/trust/UI. Reversing that order would recreate the stack’s problem—each layer inventing temporary predicates that later layers must unwind.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787608600726,"completed_at_ms":1787608601717}}
