{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:00:11.291Z","ordinal":9931,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbe6f7a1c87d09e9a6bc52a21ebcb","status":"completed","call_id":"call_1WiBRCni2bQrjNdUa2ZCqrNs","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md\\n+# Settings-Only Global Tracking Refactor Implementation Plan\\n+\\n+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\\n+\\n+**Goal:** Replace the stacked global-enable implementation with one coherent policy-and-routing architecture while preserving pre-push trust, checkpoint egress, and the complete Claude Code and Gemini CLI hook behavior.\\n+\\n+**Architecture:** A leaf package under `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy` owns user-global settings, repository policy classification, machine-local activation, immutable runtime routing, and trust identity. Existing `settings` APIs become compatibility facades while consumers migrate to one immutable `RepoPolicy` snapshot. Runtime routing is sticky per worktree, lazy setup is component-versioned, and the old enable/wizard/takeover migration paths are deleted.\\n+\\n+**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, Cobra, Charm `huh`, go-git v6, repository `flock` and `jsonutil` helpers, table-driven Go tests, integration-tag tests, Vogon deterministic E2E canary.\\n+\\n+---\\n+\\n+## Scope and execution notes\\n+\\n+- Work in the existing dedicated `global-settings-tier` worktree.\\n+- Preserve `bca00205a` and branch `fix/global-takeover-migration` as the stacked reference while refactoring.\\n+- The design and this plan are local artifacts under ignored `docs/superpowers`; do not add or commit them.\\n+- Do not run real-agent E2E tests. `mise run check` runs only the approved deterministic canaries.\\n+- Before writing Go in each task, search for reusable helpers with `rg` because the documented `/go:discover-related` skill is not installed in this environment.\\n+- Every top-level test and subtest uses `t.Parallel()` unless it calls `t.Chdir`, `t.Setenv`, or modifies another process-global seam.\\n+- Every Git-touching test uses `testutil.InitRepo`, repository-local identity/GPG config, and a temp worktree.\\n+- Before every commit run `mise run check`. Before any push rerun `mise run lint` after the final formatter pass.\\n+- Recorded intent from Entire checkpoints and commit history that must survive:\\n+  - the disabled/unconfigured global fast path performs no Git subprocess;\\n+  - invalid exclusions fail closed;\\n+  - global-only tracking never writes `.entire/metadata`, `logs`, or `tmp` into the worktree;\\n+  - lazy setup never turns an agent/Git hook failure into a failed host operation;\\n+  - pre-push consent remains Yes / Not now / Always and Git stdin is never used;\\n+  - Claude/Gemini user-hook installs preserve unrelated configuration and deduplicate against repo-scope production hooks.\\n+\\n+## Final file structure\\n+\\n+### New leaf policy package\\n+\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go`: immutable policy, activation, route, trust, and reason types.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings.go`: strict user settings schema, loading, validation, locking, and atomic writes.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository.go`: Git/worktree facts and stable worktree namespace resolution without importing `paths` or parent `settings`.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`: project-settings provenance, activation marker, legacy bootstrap, and disable tombstone.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`: route registry, atomic first-writer-wins selection, and policy context memo.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`: read-only `ClassifyRepoPolicy` and mutating `EnsureRuntimeRoute` orchestration.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`: trust identity, egress decision, trust writers, and grant ledger.\\n+- Matching focused `_test.go` files beside each responsibility.\\n+\\n+### Existing packages\\n+\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go`: shrink to aliases/facades plus public diagnostics helpers; no independent policy tree.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`: shrink to compatibility facades or delete once callers use `repopolicy`.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go`: construct runtime paths from a resolved route; delete settings parsing and activation mirrors.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`: retain user-hook reconciliation helpers only; delete global activation commands, wizard, and runtime migration.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go`: component-versioned lazy Git setup consuming `RepoPolicy`.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/{claudecode,geminicli}/hooks*.go`: declarative hook specs shared by repo/user install, detection, removal, and diagnostics.\\n+- `cmd/entire/cli/{root,hook_registry,hooks_git_cmd,lifecycle,status,doctor,setup}.go`: resolve/pass one policy snapshot and preserve user surfaces.\\n+\\n+---\\n+\\n+### Task 1: Establish the leaf policy model and user-settings authority\\n+\\n+**Files:**\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings_test.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_validate.go`\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 1: Search for reusable primitives and record the dependency boundary**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+rg -n \\\"ModifyUserSettings|WriteFileAtomicFollowingSymlinks|Normalize.*Origin|GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet|GetRemotePushURLsInDirIfSet|HashWorktreeID|GetWorktreeID\\\" cmd/entire/cli internal\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: reuse `jsonutil` atomic writes, `flock`, `gitremote`, and the existing worktree-ID algorithm; `repopolicy` must not import `paths`, parent `settings`, `session`, `strategy`, or `logging`.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing schema and fast-path tests**\\n+\\n+Cover:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+func TestLoadUserSettings_MissingMalformedAndStrict(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestClassifyGlobalConfig_DisabledDoesNotResolveRepository(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestValidateGlobalConfig_InvalidExclusionsFailClosed(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestModifyUserSettings_ConcurrentTrustWritesDoNotClobber(t *testing.T)\\n+```\\n+\\n+The disabled/unconfigured test injects a repository resolver that fails the test if called.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 3: Run the tests and verify they fail for the missing package**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy -run 'Test(LoadUserSettings|ClassifyGlobalConfig|ValidateGlobalConfig|ModifyUserSettings)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: FAIL because the new APIs do not exist.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Implement the minimal immutable types and settings store**\\n+\\n+Use these public shapes:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+type ActivationSource string\\n+\\n+const (\\n+\\tActivationInactive ActivationSource = \\\"inactive\\\"\\n+\\tActivationLocal    ActivationSource = \\\"local\\\"\\n+\\tActivationGlobal   ActivationSource = \\\"global\\\"\\n+)\\n+\\n+type RuntimeLayout string\\n+\\n+const (\\n+\\tRuntimeUnknown   RuntimeLayout = \\\"\\\"\\n+\\tRuntimeWorktree  RuntimeLayout = \\\"worktree\\\"\\n+\\tRuntimeGitCommon RuntimeLayout = \\\"git_common\\\"\\n+)\\n+\\n+type RepoPolicy struct {\\n+\\tActive           bool\\n+\\tActivationSource ActivationSource\\n+\\tInactiveReason   InactiveReason\\n+\\tWorktreeRoot     string\\n+\\tGitCommonDir     string\\n+\\tWorktreeKey      string\\n+\\tRoute            RuntimeRoute\\n+\\tTrust            TrustDecision\\n+}\\n+\\n+type UserSettings struct {\\n+\\tGlobal *GlobalConfig `json:\\\"global,omitempty\\\"`\\n+}\\n+```\\n+\\n+Keep the existing JSON field names and strict decoding. Keep `ModifyUserSettings` as the only writer primitive and clear only package-owned memos after persistence.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Convert the parent settings package to aliases/facades**\\n+\\n+The facade should preserve current call sites during migration:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+type GlobalConfig = repopolicy.GlobalConfig\\n+type UserSettings = repopolicy.UserSettings\\n+\\n+var LoadUserSettings = repopolicy.LoadUserSettings\\n+var ModifyUserSettings = repopolicy.ModifyUserSettings\\n+```\\n+\\n+Move validation and normalization into the leaf package instead of leaving a second implementation in `settings`.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused and parent-package tests**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings -run 'Test(Global|LoadUserSettings|ModifyUserSettings|ValidateGlobal)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: PASS.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\\n+\\n+Run: `mise run check`\\n+\\n+Expected: formatting, lint, unit/integration tests, and deterministic canaries PASS.\\n+\\n+Commit:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_validate.go\\n+git commit -m \\\"refactor(settings): centralize global repository policy inputs\\\"\\n+```\\n+\\n+---\\n+\\n+### Task 2: Add machine-local activation provenance and sticky runtime routing\\n+\\n+**Files:**\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation_test.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route_test.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/paths.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/worktree.go`\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing activation-provenance tests**\\n+\\n+Cover the exact matrix:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+func TestClassifyRepoPolicy_CommittedEnabledSettingDoesNotActivateFreshClone(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestClassifyRepoPolicy_LocalMarkerActivatesOnlyItsWorktree(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestClassifyRepoPolicy_DisabledMarkerVetoesGlobalActivation(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_SingleWorktreeRequiresVerifiedEvidence(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_LinkedWorktreeRejectsSharedHookEvidence(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_RejectsTrackedOrSymlinkedEvidence(t *testing.T)\\n+```\\n+\\n+Accepted legacy evidence is only an exact-worktree active session record or one of the recognized, untracked, non-symlinked `.entire/metadata/<session-id>/` files named in the spec.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 2: Run the activation tests and verify failure**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy -run 'Test(ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: FAIL because activation records are not implemented.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement activation records**\\n+\\n+Store one record per worktree at:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+<git-common-dir>/entire/worktrees/<worktree-key>/activation.json\\n+```\\n+\\n+Use a versioned record:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+type ActivationRecord struct {\\n+\\tVersion int             `json:\\\"version\\\"`\\n+\\tState   ActivationState `json:\\\"state\\\"`\\n+}\\n+```\\n+\\n+Writes are atomic and machine-local. `entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt records fail closed and are recoverable only through explicit enable.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Write failing route-selection tests**\\n+\\n+Cover:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+func TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_GlobalFirstSelectsGitCommonAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ExplicitFirstSelectsWorktreeAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_LinkedWorktreesAreIndependent(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestClassifyRepoPolicy_ReadOnlyDoesNotCreateRegistry(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_CorruptRecordFailsClosed(t *testing.T)\\n+```\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\\n+\\n+Store:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+<git-common-dir>/entire/worktrees/<worktree-key>/route.json\\n+```\\n+\\n+Use:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+type RuntimeRoute struct {\\n+\\tVersion int           `json:\\\"version\\\"`\\n+\\tLayout  RuntimeLayout `json:\\\"layout\\\"`\\n+}\\n+\\n+func ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, error)\\n+func EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) (RepoPolicy, error)\\n+func WithRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) context.Context\\n+func RepoPolicyFromContext(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, bool)\\n+```\\n+\\n+The creation critical section covers only read/create/publish. Write and fsync a complete temp file, publish without replacing an existing record, then reread the winner. Never hold this lock around hooks, prompts, Git operations, condensation, or runtime writes.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\\n+\\n+`paths.AbsPath` should obtain a policy snapshot from context or call read-only classification as a compatibility fallback, then map only `metadata`, `logs`, and `tmp` through the selected route. Delete `repoActivationConfigured`, `userGlobalTierEnabled`, and duplicated JSON/settings parsing from `paths/invisible.go`.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Run focused route/path tests**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: PASS, including cancellation and separate-git-dir coverage.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 8: Run duplication checks before commit**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+mise run dup\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: no new actionable duplication between `repopolicy` and `paths`.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 9: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\\n+\\n+Run: `mise run check`\\n+\\n+Commit:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/paths\\n+git commit -m \\\"refactor(global): make activation and runtime routing sticky\\\"\\n+```\\n+\\n+---\\n+\\n+### Task 3: Remove global activation commands, wizard, and takeover migration\\n+\\n+**Files:**\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root_test.go` if present; otherwise the nearest root/help test file\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup_test.go`\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing command-surface tests**\\n+\\n+Add tests asserting:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+func TestEnableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestDisableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestSetupFlow_DoesNotAskGlobalTrackingQuestion(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestRootHelp_DoesNotAdvertiseGlobalActivationFlags(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestUserFacingStrings_DoNotReferenceRemovedGlobalFlags(t *testing.T)\\n+```\\n+\\n+The repository-wide string test scans user-facing Go strings and docs but excludes historical specs/checkpoints.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 2: Run and observe failures against the current stack**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EnableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag|DisableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag|SetupFlow_DoesNotAskGlobalTrackingQuestion|RootHelp_DoesNotAdvertiseGlobalActivationFlags|UserFacingStrings)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: FAIL on flags, wizard, hints, doctor text, and docs.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 3: Delete activation mutation surfaces**\\n+\\n+Remove:\\n+\\n+- `runEnableGlobalMode` and `runDisableGlobalMode`;\\n+- both `--global` flags and mutual-exclusion wiring;\\n+- `maybePromptGlobalTracking`, configured/unconfigured ask-once state, and global tracking hints;\\n+- every user message telling the user to run either removed flag.\\n+\\n+Do not remove `entire trust`, `entire trust --revoke`, or the pre-push trust prompt.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Delete takeover migration**\\n+\\n+Remove from `setup_global.go` and callers:\\n+\\n+- migration planning and traversal;\\n+- migration lock/gate;\\n+- file move/copy helpers introduced solely for takeover;\\n+- transcript path rewriting;\\n+- retry/marker clearing used only to trigger migration.\\n+\\n+Keep generic atomic JSON helpers and any independently used hook-install lock.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Wire explicit enable/disable to activation and route**\\n+\\n+The order for `entire enable` is:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+p, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\\n+p, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\\n+err = persistRepoSettings(...)\\n+err = repopolicy.SetLocalActivation(ctx, repopolicy.ActivationEnabled)\\n+```\\n+\\n+Use the routed policy context for subsequent setup. On partial failure, return an actionable error and leave capture fail-closed. `entire disable` records a per-worktree disabled marker and preserves the route; `--uninstall` removes runtime/route data but retains the disabled tombstone.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Replace the clone-wide setup boolean with component state**\\n+\\n+Replace `ClonePreferences.GlobalSetupCompleted` with a per-worktree component record under the registry, for example:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+type SetupRecord struct {\\n+\\tVersion       int `json:\\\"version\\\"`\\n+\\tGitHooksSpec  int `json:\\\"git_hooks_spec\\\"`\\n+\\tPrimaryRefSpec int `json:\\\"primary_ref_spec\\\"`\\n+}\\n+```\\n+\\n+`MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup` repairs only stale/missing components, remains silent inside hooks, and does not mark an unsafe worktree-resident `core.hooksPath` as installed.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Run focused setup tests**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(Enable|Disable|SetupFlow|RootHelp|UserFacingStrings|MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup|EnsureSetupForHook)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: PASS; no migration tests or symbols remain.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 8: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\\n+\\n+Run: `mise run check`\\n+\\n+Commit:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git add cmd/entire/cli/setup.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_test.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup_test.go\\n+git commit -m \\\"refactor(global): make activation settings-only\\\"\\n+```\\n+\\n+---\\n+\\n+### Task 4: Preserve and harden trust plus checkpoint egress\\n+\\n+**Files:**\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust_test.go`\\n+- Modify or delete after facade migration: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go`\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing trust-identity and ledger tests**\\n+\\n+Cover:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+func TestEgressDecision_RequiresEveryFetchAndPushURL(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestEgressDecision_UnparseableConfiguredOriginHolds(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestEgressDecision_PathAppliesOnlyWhenOriginAbsent(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestTrustGrant_OriginPathOriginRemovesOnlyRecordedStaleKeys(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestTrustRevoke_PathOriginPathRemovesEveryRecordedIdentity(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestTrustRevoke_PreservesHandAuthoredUnrelatedEntries(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent(t *testing.T)\\n+```\\n+\\n+Store the trust-grant ledger machine-locally under the same per-worktree registry. It records only keys written by CLI/prompt consent so hand-authored settings are not guessed or deleted.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing pre-push behavior tests**\\n+\\n+Pin all observable outcomes:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+func TestPrePushTrust_NoPendingCheckpointDoesNotPrompt(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestPrePushTrust_YesPersistsRepoTrustRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestPrePushTrust_NotNowHoldsAndPushContinues(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestPrePushTrust_AlwaysPersistsTrustAllRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestPrePushTrust_NonInteractiveHoldsWithoutReadingStdin(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestPrePushTrust_PromptOrWriteFailureHoldsWithoutFailingGitPush(t *testing.T)\\n+```\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 3: Run and verify failures**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|TrustGrant|TrustRevoke|PrePushTrust)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: FAIL on stale identity cleanup, accessible prompt handling, or the new policy API.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Implement one trust decision tree**\\n+\\n+`RepoPolicy.Trust` must carry state and source, not a reusable grant boolean:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+type TrustDecision struct {\\n+\\tAllowed bool\\n+\\tSource  TrustSource\\n+\\tReason  TrustReason\\n+\\tIdentity TrustIdentity\\n+}\\n+```\\n+\\n+After Yes or Always persists consent, rerun `ClassifyRepoPolicy`; never continue using the pre-write decision. Every other egress entry point consumes the same decision without prompting.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve the three-choice prompt safely**\\n+\\n+Keep the existing labels and effects. Read from `/dev/tty` through the repository interactive helper, never Git stdin. In accessible mode require an explicit supported choice; otherwise return held. Abort/error means Not now semantically, logs the operational failure, and does not fail the branch push.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused trust and push tests**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|Trust|Revoke|PrePush|CheckpointSync)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: PASS.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\\n+\\n+Run: `mise run check`\\n+\\n+Commit:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go\\n+git commit -m \\\"fix(global): preserve trust while hardening checkpoint egress\\\"\\n+```\\n+\\n+---\\n+\\n+### Task 5: Make Claude and Gemini hook definitions declarative without changing behavior\\n+\\n+**Files:**\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/user_hooks.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 1: Write contract tests before refactoring implementation**\\n+\\n+Claude must retain exactly these eight entries:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+SessionStart\\n+SessionEnd\\n+Stop\\n+SubagentStop\\n+UserPromptSubmit\\n+PreToolUse[Agent]\\n+PostToolUse[Agent]\\n+PostToolUse[TaskCreate|TaskUpdate]\\n+```\\n+\\n+Gemini must retain exactly twelve entries:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+SessionStart\\n+SessionEnd[exit]\\n+SessionEnd[logout]\\n+BeforeAgent\\n+AfterAgent\\n+BeforeModel\\n+AfterModel\\n+BeforeToolSelection\\n+BeforeTool[*]\\n+AfterTool[*]\\n+PreCompress\\n+Notification\\n+```\\n+\\n+Test both repo and user scopes, current production commands, matchers, unrelated-entry preservation, partial-install repair, legacy Entire-entry replacement, and cross-scope dedup assumptions.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 2: Run hook contract tests before changing code**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run 'Test.*Hooks' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: existing tests PASS; newly added exact-inventory tests provide the behavior baseline.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 3: Introduce one declarative spec per agent**\\n+\\n+Use each agent's existing typed hook model. The spec must drive:\\n+\\n+- repo-scope installation;\\n+- user-scope installation;\\n+- currentness/completeness checks;\\n+- recognized Entire-entry removal;\\n+- expected counts for status/doctor.\\n+\\n+Do not create one lossy generic JSON schema across agents. Share orchestration, not agent-specific serialization.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Preserve no-op Gemini events**\\n+\\n+Do not remove `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, or `Notification`, even though their parser currently returns no lifecycle event. Their installed presence and command behavior are part of the product contract.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile hooks as infrastructure**\\n+\\n+User-hook reconciliation runs only from installer/update integration, `entire enable`, `entire agent add`, and confirmed doctor repair. It does not run inside hooks or read-only commands. Installation errors warn without changing global activation policy.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Run agent tests and duplication check**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli ./cmd/entire/cli/agent -count=1\\n+mise run dup\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: exact inventory unchanged and repeated install/detect/remove loops eliminated or justified.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\\n+\\n+Run: `mise run check`\\n+\\n+Commit:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git add cmd/entire/cli/agent cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go\\n+git commit -m \\\"refactor(agents): declare user hook contracts once\\\"\\n+```\\n+\\n+---\\n+\\n+### Task 6: Thread one policy snapshot through hooks and diagnostics\\n+\\n+**Files:**\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/config.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go`\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing single-classification tests**\\n+\\n+Inject a counting classifier and assert one evaluation per process flow:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+func TestAgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestGitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestStatus_ReadOnlyClassificationCreatesNoFiles(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestDoctor_ReadOnlyScanDoesNotMutatePolicyOrHooksWithoutConfirmation(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation(t *testing.T)\\n+```\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 2: Run and verify failures**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(AgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|GitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|Status_ReadOnly|Doctor_ReadOnly|HookPolicyFailure)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: FAIL while consumers independently call settings gates and path probes.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 3: Classify at hook entry and pass the snapshot through context**\\n+\\n+For runtime-writing hooks:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+p, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\\n+if err != nil || !p.Active { return nil }\\n+p, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\\n+if err != nil { logAndSkip(); return nil }\\n+ctx = repopolicy.WithRepoPolicy(ctx, p)\\n+```\\n+\\n+Remove migration-gate acquisition from agent and Git hook entry points. Route failure skips Entire work but not the user's agent, commit, or branch push.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Convert status and doctor to read-only policy consumers**\\n+\\n+Status reports configured/enabled, settings path, activation source/reason, runtime layout, trust source/held state, and user-hook health. Doctor may repair hooks only on its confirmed repair path; ordinary status/help/auth/version invocations create no activation, route, setup, or agent-config files.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve privacy-critical local failures**\\n+\\n+Do not blanket-swallow existing local OPF or redaction failures. Add a regression proving a local OPF safety failure still aborts push while policy/route/setup infrastructure failures do not.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused hook/status/doctor tests**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(AgentHook|GitHook|Lifecycle|Status|Doctor|HookPolicyFailure|OPF)' -count=1\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: PASS.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\\n+\\n+Run: `mise run check`\\n+\\n+Commit:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git add cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go cmd/entire/cli/status.go cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go cmd/entire/cli/config.go cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go\\n+git commit -m \\\"refactor(global): share one policy snapshot across runtime paths\\\"\\n+```\\n+\\n+---\\n+\\n+### Task 7: Add integration coverage, remove obsolete code, and prepare the coherent PR\\n+\\n+**Files:**\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/global_enable_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_policy_test.go`\\n+- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md`\\n+- Modify: `docs/security-and-privacy.md`\\n+- Modify: `CLAUDE.md`\\n+- Delete: obsolete migration-only tests/helpers identified by `rg`\\n+- Modify: any remaining user-facing source containing removed global-activation guidance\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 1: Replace stacked integration tests with scenario tests**\\n+\\n+Create real-binary integration coverage for:\\n+\\n+1. settings-file global activation -> Claude/Gemini user hook -> hidden runtime capture;\\n+2. no pending checkpoint -> no trust prompt/output;\\n+3. pending checkpoint -> Yes drains, Not now holds, Always drains all;\\n+4. non-interactive/accessible prompt paths hold safely without Git stdin reads;\\n+5. explicit enable after global capture keeps the git-common route;\\n+6. explicit-first route remains worktree-local after global settings turn on;\\n+7. fresh clone with committed `enabled: true` gains neither local activation nor egress;\\n+8. linked worktrees receive independent activation/route records;\\n+9. tracked or symlinked `.entire` cannot unlock executable settings or egress;\\n+10. multiple fetch/push URLs require complete trust.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 2: Run integration tests and verify failures before final fixes**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+mise run test:integration\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: any remaining wiring gaps fail with a scenario name, not a low-level helper assertion.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 3: Remove obsolete symbols and duplicated tests**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+rg -n \\\"runEnableGlobalMode|runDisableGlobalMode|maybePromptGlobalTracking|maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData|migration gate|GlobalSetupCompleted|enable --global|disable --global\\\" --glob '!docs/superpowers/**'\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected after cleanup: no production symbols or user-facing instructions remain. Historical changelog text may remain only when clearly historical and not presented as current usage.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Audit test quality and duplication**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+mise run dup\\n+mise run lint:full\\n+```\\n+\\n+Delete tests that merely repeat implementation details; retain the policy matrix, race tests, security boundaries, exact hook inventories, and real-binary scenarios.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Measure the final diff budget**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git diff --shortstat origin/main...HEAD\\n+git diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD\\n+```\\n+\\n+Target: approximately 8,000–10,000 additions total, 3,500–4,500 production additions, and materially more deletions than the current stacked branch. If additions remain near 13,000, perform another reuse/test-consolidation pass before landing.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Run final verification**\\n+\\n+Run:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+mise run check\\n+mise run lint\\n+git diff --check\\n+```\\n+\\n+Expected: all PASS and worktree contains only intended source/test/doc changes. Do not run paid real-agent E2E tests.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Commit the integration and cleanup slice**\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+git add CLAUDE.md cmd/entire/cli docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md docs/security-and-privacy.md\\n+git commit -m \\\"test(global): cover settings-only tracking end to end\\\"\\n+```\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 8: Review the complete diff against `origin/main`**\\n+\\n+Use `entire:review` for intent-aware review, then `superpowers:requesting-code-review`. Address every valid finding and rerun the relevant focused test plus `mise run check` before any fixing commit.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 9: Synthesize the clean PR history**\\n+\\n+Keep a local backup ref to the implementation branch. Rebuild the final PR head directly on `origin/main` as a coherent commit series or one reviewed squash commit; verify the rebuilt tree is byte-identical to the tested implementation tree before updating PR #2030. Do not preserve the old stack's merge commits or intermediate add-then-remove behavior.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 10: Update the remote and close gates**\\n+\\n+Before the authorized remote update, run `mise run lint` again. Update `feat/global-trust` with `--force-with-lease`, update the PR/trail body to describe the single coherent feature, then wait for every repository/PR gate to reach terminal state. Compare pre/post risk and security classifications, inspect every failure/degradation, fix valid findings, and repeat until stable. Resolve trail findings only after their implementation and regression tests are present remotely.\\n+\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787608676.058964}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:00:11.395Z","ordinal":9932,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-23f882cd-2428-43b7-8cea-163fe3c231ed","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md":{"type":"add","content":"# Settings-Only Global Tracking Refactor Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Replace the stacked global-enable implementation with one coherent policy-and-routing architecture while preserving pre-push trust, checkpoint egress, and the complete Claude Code and Gemini CLI hook behavior.\n\n**Architecture:** A leaf package under `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy` owns user-global settings, repository policy classification, machine-local activation, immutable runtime routing, and trust identity. Existing `settings` APIs become compatibility facades while consumers migrate to one immutable `RepoPolicy` snapshot. Runtime routing is sticky per worktree, lazy setup is component-versioned, and the old enable/wizard/takeover migration paths are deleted.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, Cobra, Charm `huh`, go-git v6, repository `flock` and `jsonutil` helpers, table-driven Go tests, integration-tag tests, Vogon deterministic E2E canary.\n\n---\n\n## Scope and execution notes\n\n- Work in the existing dedicated `global-settings-tier` worktree.\n- Preserve `bca00205a` and branch `fix/global-takeover-migration` as the stacked reference while refactoring.\n- The design and this plan are local artifacts under ignored `docs/superpowers`; do not add or commit them.\n- Do not run real-agent E2E tests. `mise run check` runs only the approved deterministic canaries.\n- Before writing Go in each task, search for reusable helpers with `rg` because the documented `/go:discover-related` skill is not installed in this environment.\n- Every top-level test and subtest uses `t.Parallel()` unless it calls `t.Chdir`, `t.Setenv`, or modifies another process-global seam.\n- Every Git-touching test uses `testutil.InitRepo`, repository-local identity/GPG config, and a temp worktree.\n- Before every commit run `mise run check`. Before any push rerun `mise run lint` after the final formatter pass.\n- Recorded intent from Entire checkpoints and commit history that must survive:\n  - the disabled/unconfigured global fast path performs no Git subprocess;\n  - invalid exclusions fail closed;\n  - global-only tracking never writes `.entire/metadata`, `logs`, or `tmp` into the worktree;\n  - lazy setup never turns an agent/Git hook failure into a failed host operation;\n  - pre-push consent remains Yes / Not now / Always and Git stdin is never used;\n  - Claude/Gemini user-hook installs preserve unrelated configuration and deduplicate against repo-scope production hooks.\n\n## Final file structure\n\n### New leaf policy package\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go`: immutable policy, activation, route, trust, and reason types.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings.go`: strict user settings schema, loading, validation, locking, and atomic writes.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository.go`: Git/worktree facts and stable worktree namespace resolution without importing `paths` or parent `settings`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`: project-settings provenance, activation marker, legacy bootstrap, and disable tombstone.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`: route registry, atomic first-writer-wins selection, and policy context memo.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`: read-only `ClassifyRepoPolicy` and mutating `EnsureRuntimeRoute` orchestration.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`: trust identity, egress decision, trust writers, and grant ledger.\n- Matching focused `_test.go` files beside each responsibility.\n\n### Existing packages\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go`: shrink to aliases/facades plus public diagnostics helpers; no independent policy tree.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`: shrink to compatibility facades or delete once callers use `repopolicy`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go`: construct runtime paths from a resolved route; delete settings parsing and activation mirrors.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`: retain user-hook reconciliation helpers only; delete global activation commands, wizard, and runtime migration.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go`: component-versioned lazy Git setup consuming `RepoPolicy`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/{claudecode,geminicli}/hooks*.go`: declarative hook specs shared by repo/user install, detection, removal, and diagnostics.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/{root,hook_registry,hooks_git_cmd,lifecycle,status,doctor,setup}.go`: resolve/pass one policy snapshot and preserve user surfaces.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Establish the leaf policy model and user-settings authority\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_validate.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Search for reusable primitives and record the dependency boundary**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"ModifyUserSettings|WriteFileAtomicFollowingSymlinks|Normalize.*Origin|GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet|GetRemotePushURLsInDirIfSet|HashWorktreeID|GetWorktreeID\" cmd/entire/cli internal\n```\n\nExpected: reuse `jsonutil` atomic writes, `flock`, `gitremote`, and the existing worktree-ID algorithm; `repopolicy` must not import `paths`, parent `settings`, `session`, `strategy`, or `logging`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing schema and fast-path tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestLoadUserSettings_MissingMalformedAndStrict(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyGlobalConfig_DisabledDoesNotResolveRepository(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestValidateGlobalConfig_InvalidExclusionsFailClosed(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestModifyUserSettings_ConcurrentTrustWritesDoNotClobber(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nThe disabled/unconfigured test injects a repository resolver that fails the test if called.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run the tests and verify they fail for the missing package**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy -run 'Test(LoadUserSettings|ClassifyGlobalConfig|ValidateGlobalConfig|ModifyUserSettings)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL because the new APIs do not exist.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement the minimal immutable types and settings store**\n\nUse these public shapes:\n\n```go\ntype ActivationSource string\n\nconst (\n\tActivationInactive ActivationSource = \"inactive\"\n\tActivationLocal    ActivationSource = \"local\"\n\tActivationGlobal   ActivationSource = \"global\"\n)\n\ntype RuntimeLayout string\n\nconst (\n\tRuntimeUnknown   RuntimeLayout = \"\"\n\tRuntimeWorktree  RuntimeLayout = \"worktree\"\n\tRuntimeGitCommon RuntimeLayout = \"git_common\"\n)\n\ntype RepoPolicy struct {\n\tActive           bool\n\tActivationSource ActivationSource\n\tInactiveReason   InactiveReason\n\tWorktreeRoot     string\n\tGitCommonDir     string\n\tWorktreeKey      string\n\tRoute            RuntimeRoute\n\tTrust            TrustDecision\n}\n\ntype UserSettings struct {\n\tGlobal *GlobalConfig `json:\"global,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\nKeep the existing JSON field names and strict decoding. Keep `ModifyUserSettings` as the only writer primitive and clear only package-owned memos after persistence.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Convert the parent settings package to aliases/facades**\n\nThe facade should preserve current call sites during migration:\n\n```go\ntype GlobalConfig = repopolicy.GlobalConfig\ntype UserSettings = repopolicy.UserSettings\n\nvar LoadUserSettings = repopolicy.LoadUserSettings\nvar ModifyUserSettings = repopolicy.ModifyUserSettings\n```\n\nMove validation and normalization into the leaf package instead of leaving a second implementation in `settings`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused and parent-package tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings -run 'Test(Global|LoadUserSettings|ModifyUserSettings|ValidateGlobal)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nExpected: formatting, lint, unit/integration tests, and deterministic canaries PASS.\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_validate.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(settings): centralize global repository policy inputs\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Add machine-local activation provenance and sticky runtime routing\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/paths.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/worktree.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing activation-provenance tests**\n\nCover the exact matrix:\n\n```go\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_CommittedEnabledSettingDoesNotActivateFreshClone(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_LocalMarkerActivatesOnlyItsWorktree(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_DisabledMarkerVetoesGlobalActivation(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_SingleWorktreeRequiresVerifiedEvidence(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_LinkedWorktreeRejectsSharedHookEvidence(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_RejectsTrackedOrSymlinkedEvidence(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nAccepted legacy evidence is only an exact-worktree active session record or one of the recognized, untracked, non-symlinked `.entire/metadata/<session-id>/` files named in the spec.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run the activation tests and verify failure**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy -run 'Test(ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL because activation records are not implemented.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement activation records**\n\nStore one record per worktree at:\n\n```text\n<git-common-dir>/entire/worktrees/<worktree-key>/activation.json\n```\n\nUse a versioned record:\n\n```go\ntype ActivationRecord struct {\n\tVersion int             `json:\"version\"`\n\tState   ActivationState `json:\"state\"`\n}\n```\n\nWrites are atomic and machine-local. `entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt records fail closed and are recoverable only through explicit enable.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Write failing route-selection tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_GlobalFirstSelectsGitCommonAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ExplicitFirstSelectsWorktreeAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_LinkedWorktreesAreIndependent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_ReadOnlyDoesNotCreateRegistry(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_CorruptRecordFailsClosed(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\n\nStore:\n\n```text\n<git-common-dir>/entire/worktrees/<worktree-key>/route.json\n```\n\nUse:\n\n```go\ntype RuntimeRoute struct {\n\tVersion int           `json:\"version\"`\n\tLayout  RuntimeLayout `json:\"layout\"`\n}\n\nfunc ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, error)\nfunc EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) (RepoPolicy, error)\nfunc WithRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) context.Context\nfunc RepoPolicyFromContext(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, bool)\n```\n\nThe creation critical section covers only read/create/publish. Write and fsync a complete temp file, publish without replacing an existing record, then reread the winner. Never hold this lock around hooks, prompts, Git operations, condensation, or runtime writes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\n\n`paths.AbsPath` should obtain a policy snapshot from context or call read-only classification as a compatibility fallback, then map only `metadata`, `logs`, and `tmp` through the selected route. Delete `repoActivationConfigured`, `userGlobalTierEnabled`, and duplicated JSON/settings parsing from `paths/invisible.go`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run focused route/path tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS, including cancellation and separate-git-dir coverage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Run duplication checks before commit**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: no new actionable duplication between `repopolicy` and `paths`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/paths\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): make activation and runtime routing sticky\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Remove global activation commands, wizard, and takeover migration\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root_test.go` if present; otherwise the nearest root/help test file\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing command-surface tests**\n\nAdd tests asserting:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEnableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestDisableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestSetupFlow_DoesNotAskGlobalTrackingQuestion(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestRootHelp_DoesNotAdvertiseGlobalActivationFlags(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestUserFacingStrings_DoNotReferenceRemovedGlobalFlags(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nThe repository-wide string test scans user-facing Go strings and docs but excludes historical specs/checkpoints.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run and observe failures against the current stack**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EnableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag|DisableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag|SetupFlow_DoesNotAskGlobalTrackingQuestion|RootHelp_DoesNotAdvertiseGlobalActivationFlags|UserFacingStrings)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL on flags, wizard, hints, doctor text, and docs.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Delete activation mutation surfaces**\n\nRemove:\n\n- `runEnableGlobalMode` and `runDisableGlobalMode`;\n- both `--global` flags and mutual-exclusion wiring;\n- `maybePromptGlobalTracking`, configured/unconfigured ask-once state, and global tracking hints;\n- every user message telling the user to run either removed flag.\n\nDo not remove `entire trust`, `entire trust --revoke`, or the pre-push trust prompt.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Delete takeover migration**\n\nRemove from `setup_global.go` and callers:\n\n- migration planning and traversal;\n- migration lock/gate;\n- file move/copy helpers introduced solely for takeover;\n- transcript path rewriting;\n- retry/marker clearing used only to trigger migration.\n\nKeep generic atomic JSON helpers and any independently used hook-install lock.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Wire explicit enable/disable to activation and route**\n\nThe order for `entire enable` is:\n\n```go\np, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\np, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\nerr = persistRepoSettings(...)\nerr = repopolicy.SetLocalActivation(ctx, repopolicy.ActivationEnabled)\n```\n\nUse the routed policy context for subsequent setup. On partial failure, return an actionable error and leave capture fail-closed. `entire disable` records a per-worktree disabled marker and preserves the route; `--uninstall` removes runtime/route data but retains the disabled tombstone.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Replace the clone-wide setup boolean with component state**\n\nReplace `ClonePreferences.GlobalSetupCompleted` with a per-worktree component record under the registry, for example:\n\n```go\ntype SetupRecord struct {\n\tVersion       int `json:\"version\"`\n\tGitHooksSpec  int `json:\"git_hooks_spec\"`\n\tPrimaryRefSpec int `json:\"primary_ref_spec\"`\n}\n```\n\n`MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup` repairs only stale/missing components, remains silent inside hooks, and does not mark an unsafe worktree-resident `core.hooksPath` as installed.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run focused setup tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(Enable|Disable|SetupFlow|RootHelp|UserFacingStrings|MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup|EnsureSetupForHook)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS; no migration tests or symbols remain.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/setup.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_test.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup_test.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): make activation settings-only\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Preserve and harden trust plus checkpoint egress\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust_test.go`\n- Modify or delete after facade migration: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing trust-identity and ledger tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEgressDecision_RequiresEveryFetchAndPushURL(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_UnparseableConfiguredOriginHolds(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_PathAppliesOnlyWhenOriginAbsent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustGrant_OriginPathOriginRemovesOnlyRecordedStaleKeys(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PathOriginPathRemovesEveryRecordedIdentity(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PreservesHandAuthoredUnrelatedEntries(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nStore the trust-grant ledger machine-locally under the same per-worktree registry. It records only keys written by CLI/prompt consent so hand-authored settings are not guessed or deleted.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing pre-push behavior tests**\n\nPin all observable outcomes:\n\n```go\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NoPendingCheckpointDoesNotPrompt(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_YesPersistsRepoTrustRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NotNowHoldsAndPushContinues(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AlwaysPersistsTrustAllRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NonInteractiveHoldsWithoutReadingStdin(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_PromptOrWriteFailureHoldsWithoutFailingGitPush(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|TrustGrant|TrustRevoke|PrePushTrust)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL on stale identity cleanup, accessible prompt handling, or the new policy API.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement one trust decision tree**\n\n`RepoPolicy.Trust` must carry state and source, not a reusable grant boolean:\n\n```go\ntype TrustDecision struct {\n\tAllowed bool\n\tSource  TrustSource\n\tReason  TrustReason\n\tIdentity TrustIdentity\n}\n```\n\nAfter Yes or Always persists consent, rerun `ClassifyRepoPolicy`; never continue using the pre-write decision. Every other egress entry point consumes the same decision without prompting.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve the three-choice prompt safely**\n\nKeep the existing labels and effects. Read from `/dev/tty` through the repository interactive helper, never Git stdin. In accessible mode require an explicit supported choice; otherwise return held. Abort/error means Not now semantically, logs the operational failure, and does not fail the branch push.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused trust and push tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|Trust|Revoke|PrePush|CheckpointSync)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go\ngit commit -m \"fix(global): preserve trust while hardening checkpoint egress\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Make Claude and Gemini hook definitions declarative without changing behavior\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/user_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write contract tests before refactoring implementation**\n\nClaude must retain exactly these eight entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd\nStop\nSubagentStop\nUserPromptSubmit\nPreToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[TaskCreate|TaskUpdate]\n```\n\nGemini must retain exactly twelve entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd[exit]\nSessionEnd[logout]\nBeforeAgent\nAfterAgent\nBeforeModel\nAfterModel\nBeforeToolSelection\nBeforeTool[*]\nAfterTool[*]\nPreCompress\nNotification\n```\n\nTest both repo and user scopes, current production commands, matchers, unrelated-entry preservation, partial-install repair, legacy Entire-entry replacement, and cross-scope dedup assumptions.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run hook contract tests before changing code**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run 'Test.*Hooks' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: existing tests PASS; newly added exact-inventory tests provide the behavior baseline.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Introduce one declarative spec per agent**\n\nUse each agent's existing typed hook model. The spec must drive:\n\n- repo-scope installation;\n- user-scope installation;\n- currentness/completeness checks;\n- recognized Entire-entry removal;\n- expected counts for status/doctor.\n\nDo not create one lossy generic JSON schema across agents. Share orchestration, not agent-specific serialization.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Preserve no-op Gemini events**\n\nDo not remove `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, or `Notification`, even though their parser currently returns no lifecycle event. Their installed presence and command behavior are part of the product contract.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile hooks as infrastructure**\n\nUser-hook reconciliation runs only from installer/update integration, `entire enable`, `entire agent add`, and confirmed doctor repair. It does not run inside hooks or read-only commands. Installation errors warn without changing global activation policy.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run agent tests and duplication check**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli ./cmd/entire/cli/agent -count=1\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: exact inventory unchanged and repeated install/detect/remove loops eliminated or justified.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(agents): declare user hook contracts once\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Thread one policy snapshot through hooks and diagnostics\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/config.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing single-classification tests**\n\nInject a counting classifier and assert one evaluation per process flow:\n\n```go\nfunc TestAgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestGitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestStatus_ReadOnlyClassificationCreatesNoFiles(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestDoctor_ReadOnlyScanDoesNotMutatePolicyOrHooksWithoutConfirmation(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(AgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|GitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|Status_ReadOnly|Doctor_ReadOnly|HookPolicyFailure)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL while consumers independently call settings gates and path probes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Classify at hook entry and pass the snapshot through context**\n\nFor runtime-writing hooks:\n\n```go\np, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\nif err != nil || !p.Active { return nil }\np, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\nif err != nil { logAndSkip(); return nil }\nctx = repopolicy.WithRepoPolicy(ctx, p)\n```\n\nRemove migration-gate acquisition from agent and Git hook entry points. Route failure skips Entire work but not the user's agent, commit, or branch push.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Convert status and doctor to read-only policy consumers**\n\nStatus reports configured/enabled, settings path, activation source/reason, runtime layout, trust source/held state, and user-hook health. Doctor may repair hooks only on its confirmed repair path; ordinary status/help/auth/version invocations create no activation, route, setup, or agent-config files.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve privacy-critical local failures**\n\nDo not blanket-swallow existing local OPF or redaction failures. Add a regression proving a local OPF safety failure still aborts push while policy/route/setup infrastructure failures do not.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused hook/status/doctor tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(AgentHook|GitHook|Lifecycle|Status|Doctor|HookPolicyFailure|OPF)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go cmd/entire/cli/status.go cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go cmd/entire/cli/config.go cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): share one policy snapshot across runtime paths\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 7: Add integration coverage, remove obsolete code, and prepare the coherent PR\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/global_enable_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_policy_test.go`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md`\n- Modify: `docs/security-and-privacy.md`\n- Modify: `CLAUDE.md`\n- Delete: obsolete migration-only tests/helpers identified by `rg`\n- Modify: any remaining user-facing source containing removed global-activation guidance\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace stacked integration tests with scenario tests**\n\nCreate real-binary integration coverage for:\n\n1. settings-file global activation -> Claude/Gemini user hook -> hidden runtime capture;\n2. no pending checkpoint -> no trust prompt/output;\n3. pending checkpoint -> Yes drains, Not now holds, Always drains all;\n4. non-interactive/accessible prompt paths hold safely without Git stdin reads;\n5. explicit enable after global capture keeps the git-common route;\n6. explicit-first route remains worktree-local after global settings turn on;\n7. fresh clone with committed `enabled: true` gains neither local activation nor egress;\n8. linked worktrees receive independent activation/route records;\n9. tracked or symlinked `.entire` cannot unlock executable settings or egress;\n10. multiple fetch/push URLs require complete trust.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run integration tests and verify failures before final fixes**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run test:integration\n```\n\nExpected: any remaining wiring gaps fail with a scenario name, not a low-level helper assertion.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Remove obsolete symbols and duplicated tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"runEnableGlobalMode|runDisableGlobalMode|maybePromptGlobalTracking|maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData|migration gate|GlobalSetupCompleted|enable --global|disable --global\" --glob '!docs/superpowers/**'\n```\n\nExpected after cleanup: no production symbols or user-facing instructions remain. Historical changelog text may remain only when clearly historical and not presented as current usage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Audit test quality and duplication**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\nmise run lint:full\n```\n\nDelete tests that merely repeat implementation details; retain the policy matrix, race tests, security boundaries, exact hook inventories, and real-binary scenarios.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Measure the final diff budget**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngit diff --shortstat origin/main...HEAD\ngit diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD\n```\n\nTarget: approximately 8,000–10,000 additions total, 3,500–4,500 production additions, and materially more deletions than the current stacked branch. If additions remain near 13,000, perform another reuse/test-consolidation pass before landing.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run final verification**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run check\nmise run lint\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nExpected: all PASS and worktree contains only intended source/test/doc changes. Do not run paid real-agent E2E tests.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit the integration and cleanup slice**\n\n```bash\ngit add CLAUDE.md cmd/entire/cli docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md docs/security-and-privacy.md\ngit commit -m \"test(global): cover settings-only tracking end to end\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Review the complete diff against `origin/main`**\n\nUse `entire:review` for intent-aware review, then `superpowers:requesting-code-review`. Address every valid finding and rerun the relevant focused test plus `mise run check` before any fixing commit.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Synthesize the clean PR history**\n\nKeep a local backup ref to the implementation branch. Rebuild the final PR head directly on `origin/main` as a coherent commit series or one reviewed squash commit; verify the rebuilt tree is byte-identical to the tested implementation tree before updating PR #2030. Do not preserve the old stack's merge commits or intermediate add-then-remove behavior.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Update the remote and close gates**\n\nBefore the authorized remote update, run `mise run lint` again. Update `feat/global-trust` with `--force-with-lease`, update the PR/trail body to describe the single coherent feature, then wait for every repository/PR gate to reach terminal state. Compare pre/post risk and security classifications, inspect every failure/degradation, fix valid findings, and repeat until stable. Resolve trail findings only after their implementation and regression tests are present remotely.\n\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787608811310,"completed_at_ms":1787608811395}}
