ionState `json:\"state\"`\n}\n```\n\nWrites are atomic and machine-local. `entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt records fail closed and are recoverable only through explicit enable.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Write failing route-selection tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_GlobalFirstSelectsGitCommonAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ExplicitFirstSelectsWorktreeAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_LinkedWorktreesAreIndependent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_ReadOnlyDoesNotCreateRegistry(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_CorruptRecordFailsClosed(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\n\nStore:\n\n```text\n<git-common-dir>/entire/worktrees/<worktree-key>/route.json\n```\n\nUse:\n\n```go\ntype RuntimeRoute struct {\n\tVersion int           `json:\"version\"`\n\tLayout  RuntimeLayout `json:\"layout\"`\n}\n\nfunc ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, error)\nfunc EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) (RepoPolicy, error)\nfunc WithRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) context.Context\nfunc RepoPolicyFromContext(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, bool)\n```\n\nThe creation critical section covers only read/create/publish. Write and fsync a complete temp file, publish without replacing an existing record, then reread the winner. Never hold this lock around hooks, prompts, Git operations, condensation, or runtime writes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\n\n`paths.AbsPath` should obtain a policy snapshot from context or call read-only classification as a compatibility fallback, then map only `metadata`, `logs`, and `tmp` through the selected route. Delete `repoActivationConfigured`, `userGlobalTierEnabled`, and duplicated JSON/settings parsing from `paths/invisible.go`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run focused route/path tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS, including cancellation and separate-git-dir coverage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Run duplication checks before commit**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: no new actionable duplication between `repopolicy` and `paths`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/paths\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): make activation and runtime routing sticky\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Remove global activation commands, wizard, and takeover migration\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root_test.go` if present; otherwise the nearest root/help test file\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing command-surface tests**\n\nAdd tests asserting:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEnableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestDisableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestSetupFlow_DoesNotAskGlobalTrackingQuestion(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestRootHelp_DoesNotAdvertiseGlobalActivationFlags(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestUserFacingStrings_DoNotReferenceRemovedGlobalFlags(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nThe repository-wide string test scans user-facing Go strings and docs but excludes historical specs/checkpoints.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run and observe failures against the current stack**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EnableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag|DisableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag|SetupFlow_DoesNotAskGlobalTrackingQuestion|RootHelp_DoesNotAdvertiseGlobalActivationFlags|UserFacingStrings)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL on flags, wizard, hints, doctor text, and docs.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Delete activation mutation surfaces**\n\nRemove:\n\n- `runEnableGlobalMode` and `runDisableGlobalMode`;\n- both `--global` flags and mutual-exclusion wiring;\n- `maybePromptGlobalTracking`, configured/unconfigured ask-once state, and global tracking hints;\n- every user message telling the user to run either removed flag.\n"},"started_at_ms":1787608863087,"completed_at_ms":1787608863087}}
