{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:01:14.502Z","ordinal":9969,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbf20f23887d08c1baaf747a96ad1","status":"completed","call_id":"call_doPdpzrtFSEVQxseTgBPngty","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md\\n@@\\n - Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`\\n - Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation_test.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance.go`\\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance_test.go`\\n@@\\n Writes are atomic and machine-local. `entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt records fail closed and are recoverable only through explicit enable.\\n \\n-- [ ] **Step 4: Write failing route-selection tests**\\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Write and implement the hook-settings provenance boundary**\\n+\\n+Cover a fresh clone whose tracked or symlink-traversing `.entire` contains\\n+malicious values for OPF commands, checkpoint destination, external agents,\\n+absolute hook path, strategy options, commit linking, signing, and Vercel.\\n+Under global-only activation none may influence hook execution or egress.\\n+Built-in declarative redaction remains available, and locally activated\\n+repositories retain the existing per-field provenance behavior.\\n+\\n+Implement a positive whitelist:\\n+\\n+```go\\n+type HookSettings struct {\\n+\\tLogLevel          string\\n+\\tPII               bool\\n+\\tCustomRedactions  []string\\n+\\tExternalizeImages bool\\n+}\\n+\\n+func LoadHookSettings(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) (HookSettings, error)\\n+```\\n+\\n+Validation starts at the canonical worktree root and `lstat`s each\\n+worktree-relative `.entire/settings*.json` path component. Never derive the\\n+relative path from an already attacker-controlled symlink target.\\n+\\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Write failing route-selection tests**\\n@@\\n-- [ ] **Step 5: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\\n@@\\n-- [ ] **Step 6: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\\n@@\\n-- [ ] **Step 7: Run focused route/path tests**\\n+- [ ] **Step 8: Run focused route/path tests**\\n@@\\n-go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|LoadHookSettings|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\\n@@\\n-- [ ] **Step 8: Run duplication checks before commit**\\n+- [ ] **Step 9: Run duplication checks before commit**\\n@@\\n-- [ ] **Step 9: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\\n+- [ ] **Step 10: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787608864.058927}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:01:14.619Z","ordinal":9970,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-94508def-23f8-4c20-a527-c64e3d85064d","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -183,2 +183,4 @@\n - Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation_test.go`\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance.go`\n+- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance_test.go`\n - Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`\n@@ -236,4 +238,30 @@\n \n-- [ ] **Step 4: Write failing route-selection tests**\n+- [ ] **Step 4: Write and implement the hook-settings provenance boundary**\n+\n+Cover a fresh clone whose tracked or symlink-traversing `.entire` contains\n+malicious values for OPF commands, checkpoint destination, external agents,\n+absolute hook path, strategy options, commit linking, signing, and Vercel.\n+Under global-only activation none may influence hook execution or egress.\n+Built-in declarative redaction remains available, and locally activated\n+repositories retain the existing per-field provenance behavior.\n+\n+Implement a positive whitelist:\n \n+```go\n+type HookSettings struct {\n+\tLogLevel          string\n+\tPII               bool\n+\tCustomRedactions  []string\n+\tExternalizeImages bool\n+}\n+\n+func LoadHookSettings(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) (HookSettings, error)\n+```\n+\n+Validation starts at the canonical worktree root and `lstat`s each\n+worktree-relative `.entire/settings*.json` path component. Never derive the\n+relative path from an already attacker-controlled symlink target.\n+\n+- [ ] **Step 5: Write failing route-selection tests**\n+\n Cover:\n@@ -249,3 +277,3 @@\n \n-- [ ] **Step 5: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\n+- [ ] **Step 6: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\n \n@@ -273,3 +301,3 @@\n \n-- [ ] **Step 6: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\n+- [ ] **Step 7: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\n \n@@ -277,3 +305,3 @@\n \n-- [ ] **Step 7: Run focused route/path tests**\n+- [ ] **Step 8: Run focused route/path tests**\n \n@@ -282,3 +310,3 @@\n ```bash\n-go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\n+go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|LoadHookSettings|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\n ```\n@@ -287,3 +315,3 @@\n \n-- [ ] **Step 8: Run duplication checks before commit**\n+- [ ] **Step 9: Run duplication checks before commit**\n \n@@ -297,3 +325,3 @@\n \n-- [ ] **Step 9: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n+- [ ] **Step 10: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n \n@@ -803,2 +831 @@\n Before the authorized remote update, run `mise run lint` again. Update `feat/global-trust` with `--force-with-lease`, update the PR/trail body to describe the single coherent feature, then wait for every repository/PR gate to reach terminal state. Compare pre/post risk and security classifications, inspect every failure/degradation, fix valid findings, and repeat until stable. Resolve trail findings only after their implementation and regression tests are present remotely.\n-\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787608874548,"completed_at_ms":1787608874619}}
