{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:03:45.707Z","ordinal":10004,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a035cd-0cab-77b0-93f1-83a1ddf8c5a1","author":"/root/plan_document_reviewer","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan_document_reviewer\nPayload:\n## Plan Review\n**Status:** Issues Found\n**Issues (if any):**\n- [Task 2, Steps 3 and 6]: The plan uses `<git-common-dir>/entire/worktrees/...` and records only version/layout, while the spec and existing hidden runtime use `entire/worktree/...` and require full canonical worktree and Git-common identities verified on every read, with `0600` files under `0700` directories. - The proposed layout could orphan existing runtime data and leaves short-hash collisions and marker permissions unresolved.\n- [Task 2, Step 4; Task 6, Step 3]: The hook-settings whitelist is neither compatible with the existing settings model nor wired into hook consumers. `PII bool` loses category/custom-pattern settings, `CustomRedactions []string` conflicts with the existing `map[string]string`, malformed allowed values and exhaustive classification of every `EntireSettings` field are not tested, and no step replaces hook-path `settings.Load` calls with the sanitized view. - The symlink/executable-settings finding can remain exploitable even if the new helper’s direct tests pass.\n- [Task 4, Steps 1–6]: No test asserts that `global.enabled: false` remains inactive and denies egress when `trust_all: true`. - This is the required regression for trail finding `01M0TSGEJB4B513AV3TS310RN0`, so the plan does not yet cover all eight findings.\n**Recommendations (advisory, do not block approval):**\n- Add a compact finding-to-regression checklist so each trail finding can be verified before resolution."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787609025.707539}}}
