{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:04:29.311Z","ordinal":10029,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbfe72a2c87d092ef29fac7847f61","status":"completed","call_id":"call_tSSrIdXcsl7hiBZZouUkYtcM","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md\\n@@\\n-Writes are atomic and machine-local. `entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt records fail closed and are recoverable only through explicit enable.\\n+Writes are atomic `0600` files under the same `0700` per-worktree registry and\\n+are machine-local. Each record carries and verifies the full canonical\\n+worktree/Git-common identities in addition to its schema version and state.\\n+`entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt,\\n+unknown-version, or identity-mismatched records fail closed and are recoverable\\n+only through explicit enable.\\n@@\\n func TestEgressDecision_PathAppliesOnlyWhenOriginAbsent(t *testing.T)\\n+func TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue(t *testing.T)\\n func TestTrustGrant_OriginPathOriginRemovesOnlyRecordedStaleKeys(t *testing.T)\\n@@\\n - [ ] **Step 3: Classify at hook entry and pass the snapshot through context**\\n@@\\n Remove migration-gate acquisition from agent and Git hook entry points. Route failure skips Entire work but not the user's agent, commit, or branch push.\\n+\\n+After storing the snapshot in context, make `settings.Load(ctx)` delegate to\\n+`LoadForRepoPolicy` whenever that context contains a policy. Audit every\\n+hook-reachable `settings.Load` call in `strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`,\\n+`strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`,\\n+`strategy/manual_commit_push.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`,\\n+`strategy/hooks.go`, `strategy/common.go`, and lifecycle/state capture. Add\\n+consumer-level tests proving malicious ignored values cannot select an OPF\\n+command, checkpoint remote/backend, external agent, hook path, signing mode, or\\n+commit-linking behavior. Foreground commands running without a policy snapshot\\n+retain the existing full settings behavior.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787609061.9947}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:04:29.420Z","ordinal":10030,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-b8cebe69-8372-473a-bfa6-1f38ec6cbded","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -244,3 +244,8 @@\n \n-Writes are atomic and machine-local. `entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt records fail closed and are recoverable only through explicit enable.\n+Writes are atomic `0600` files under the same `0700` per-worktree registry and\n+are machine-local. Each record carries and verifies the full canonical\n+worktree/Git-common identities in addition to its schema version and state.\n+`entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt,\n+unknown-version, or identity-mismatched records fail closed and are recoverable\n+only through explicit enable.\n \n@@ -498,2 +503,3 @@\n func TestEgressDecision_PathAppliesOnlyWhenOriginAbsent(t *testing.T)\n+func TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue(t *testing.T)\n func TestTrustGrant_OriginPathOriginRemovesOnlyRecordedStaleKeys(t *testing.T)\n@@ -737,2 +743,13 @@\n \n+After storing the snapshot in context, make `settings.Load(ctx)` delegate to\n+`LoadForRepoPolicy` whenever that context contains a policy. Audit every\n+hook-reachable `settings.Load` call in `strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`,\n+`strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`,\n+`strategy/manual_commit_push.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`,\n+`strategy/hooks.go`, `strategy/common.go`, and lifecycle/state capture. Add\n+consumer-level tests proving malicious ignored values cannot select an OPF\n+command, checkpoint remote/backend, external agent, hook path, signing mode, or\n+commit-linking behavior. Foreground commands running without a policy snapshot\n+retain the existing full settings behavior.\n+\n - [ ] **Step 4: Convert status and doctor to read-only policy consumers**\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787609069353,"completed_at_ms":1787609069420}}
