{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:08:58.788Z","ordinal":10131,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-94ac8074-8313-4102-b596-5bbe18cb6c09","process_id":"72364","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '775,850p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '775,850p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md","name":"2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md","path":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"- [ ] **Step 2: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(AgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|GitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|Status_ReadOnly|Doctor_ReadOnly|HookPolicyFailure)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL while consumers independently call settings gates and path probes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Classify at hook entry and pass the snapshot through context**\n\nFor runtime-writing hooks:\n\n```go\np, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\nif err != nil || !p.Active { return nil }\np, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\nif err != nil { logAndSkip(); return nil }\nctx = repopolicy.WithRepoPolicy(ctx, p)\n```\n\nRemove migration-gate acquisition from agent and Git hook entry points. Route failure skips Entire work but not the user's agent, commit, or branch push.\n\nAfter storing the snapshot in context, make `settings.Load(ctx)` delegate to\n`LoadForRepoPolicy` whenever that context contains a policy. Audit every\nhook-reachable `settings.Load` call in `strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`,\n`strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`,\n`strategy/manual_commit_push.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`,\n`strategy/hooks.go`, `strategy/common.go`, and lifecycle/state capture. Add\nconsumer-level tests proving malicious ignored values cannot select an OPF\ncommand, checkpoint remote/backend, external agent, hook path, signing mode, or\ncommit-linking behavior. Foreground commands running without a policy snapshot\nretain the existing full settings behavior.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Convert status and doctor to read-only policy consumers**\n\nStatus reports configured/enabled, settings path, activation source/reason, runtime layout, trust source/held state, and user-hook health. Doctor may repair hooks only on its confirmed repair path; ordinary status/help/auth/version invocations create no activation, route, setup, or agent-config files.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve privacy-critical local failures**\n\nDo not blanket-swallow existing local OPF or redaction failures. Add a regression proving a local OPF safety failure still aborts push while policy/route/setup infrastructure failures do not.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused hook/status/doctor tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(AgentHook|GitHook|Lifecycle|Status|Doctor|HookPolicyFailure|OPF)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go cmd/entire/cli/status.go cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go cmd/entire/cli/config.go cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go cmd/entire/cli/settings cmd/entire/cli/strategy\ngi