{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:11:55.447Z","ordinal":10207,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cc1a936d487d0a7b4a07b07b3acb1","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nTask 1 creates a dependency “leaf”: repository policy can depend on Git/config primitives, while the broader CLI depends on repository policy. That direction prevents the current activation, routing, and trust logic from forming import cycles.\n\nThe parent `settings` package will remain the compatibility boundary, so this first commit should reorganize authority without changing user-visible behavior.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nI’m starting the first implementation task now: centralize the global repository-policy inputs, preserve the existing APIs through facades, and prove the move with focused concurrency and fail-closed tests."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787609513241,"completed_at_ms":1787609515447}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:11:55.448Z","ordinal":10208,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cc1a936d487d0a7b4a07b07b3acb1","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nTask 1 creates a dependency “leaf”: repository policy can depend on Git/config primitives, while the broader CLI depends on repository policy. That direction prevents the current activation, routing, and trust logic from forming import cycles.\n\nThe parent `settings` package will remain the compatibility boundary, so this first commit should reorganize authority without changing user-visible behavior.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nI’m starting the first implementation task now: centralize the global repository-policy inputs, preserve the existing APIs through facades, and prove the move with focused concurrency and fail-closed tests."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787609512.186832}}}
