{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T23:31:23.288Z","ordinal":10872,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a0361d-4618-7d42-b025-d60e3d7237e5","author":"/root/task1_quality_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/task1_quality_review\nPayload:\n### Strengths\n\n- Both prior Important issues are fixed with meaningful regression tests:\n  - Strict loading now rejects trailing junk and additional JSON values.\n  - Unnormalizable origins no longer expose raw URLs or credentials.\n- The detailed `GlobalConfig` field contracts were restored in the leaf package.\n- The full range retains the intended dependency direction, compatibility facades, lazy Git resolution, fail-closed classification, atomic locked mutation, and shared worktree identity logic.\n- Focused package tests, the `repopolicy` race test, `git diff --check`, and Windows cross-compilation passed.\n\n### Issues\n\n#### Critical\n\nNone.\n\n#### Important\n\nNone.\n\n#### Minor\n\nNone.\n\n### Recommendations\n\n- Non-blocking future coverage could include full `ResolveRepositoryAt` tests for symlinked roots and separate Git directories, plus a golden JSON-contract test.\n\n### Assessment\n\nReady to proceed? Yes. The prior findings are correctly resolved, their regression tests exercise the actual failure modes, and the fix commit introduces no new production-readiness concerns."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787614283.288944}}}
