{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T23:31:33.236Z","ordinal":10884,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3ce36f1f-529b-499f-8bf5-bf1ed2689977","process_id":"84963","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '185,385p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '185,385p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md","name":"2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md","path":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"### Task 2: Add machine-local activation provenance and sticky runtime routing\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/paths.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/worktree.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing activation-provenance tests**\n\nCover the exact matrix:\n\n```go\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_CommittedEnabledSettingDoesNotActivateFreshClone(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_LocalMarkerActivatesOnlyItsWorktree(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_DisabledMarkerVetoesGlobalActivation(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_SingleWorktreeRequiresVerifiedEvidence(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_LinkedWorktreeRejectsSharedHookEvidence(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_RejectsTrackedOrSymlinkedEvidence(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nAccepted legacy evidence is only an exact-worktree active session record or one of the recognized, untracked, non-symlinked `.entire/metadata/<session-id>/` files named in the spec.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run the activation tests and verify failure**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy -run 'Test(ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL because activation records are not implemented.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement activation records**\n\nStore one record per worktree at:\n\n```text\n<git-common-dir>/entire/worktree/<worktree-key>/activation.json\n```\n\nUse a versioned record:\n\n```go\ntype ActivationRecord struct {\n\tVersion            int             `json:\"version\"`\n\tState              ActivationState `json:\"state\"`\n\tCanonicalWorktree  string          `json:\"canonical_worktree\"`\n\tCanonicalGitCommon string          `json:\"canonical_git_common\"`\n}\n```\n\nWrites are atomic `0600` files under the same `0700` per-worktree registry and\nare machine-local. Each record carries and verifies the full canonical\nworktree/Git-common identities in addition to its schema version and state.\n`entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt,\nunknown-version, or identity-mismatched records fail closed and are recoverable\nonly through explicit enable.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Write failing hook-settings provenance tests**\n\nThe leaf package reports verified local-settings provenance; the parent\n`settings` package builds the typed sanitized view so it can preserve the exact\nexisting field shapes. Cover a fresh clone whose tracked or symlink-traversing `.entire` contains\nmalicious values for OPF commands, checkpoint destination, external agents,\nabsolute hook path, strategy options, commit linking, signing, and Vercel.\nUnder global-only activation none may influence hook execution or egress.\nBuilt-in declarative redaction remains available, and locally activated\nrepositories retain the existing per-field provenance behavior.\n\nSpecify the intended API in the test:\n\n```go\nfunc LoadForRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context, p repopolicy.RepoPolicy) (*EntireSettings, error)\n```\n\nFor global-only activation the returned `EntireSettings` copies only\n`enabled`, `log_level`, `redaction.pii` (including category pointers and\n`custom_patterns`), `redaction.custom_redactions` as its existing\n`map[string]string`, and `redaction.externalize_images`. It reconstructs the\nredaction object rather than copying scanner/OPF substructures. Malformed\nallowed fields fail closed. Local activation preserves the current merged\nloader and OPF command provenance rule.\n\nAdd an exhaustive reflection-backed test over every JSON field of\n`EntireSettings` and `RedactionSettings`: each field must appear in an explicit\nallowed-or-ignored classification table, so adding a field cannot expose it to\nglobal hooks by accident.\n\nValidation starts at the canonical worktree root and `lstat`s each\nworktree-relative `.entire/settings*.json` path component. Never derive the\nrelative path from an already attacker-controlled symlink target.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run the provenance tests and verify failure**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings -run 'Test.*(Provenance|LoadForRepoPolicy|HookFieldClassification)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL before the provenance validator and sanitized loader exist.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Implement the hook-settings provenance boundary**\n\nImplement the typed API and exhaustive classification described in Step 4,\nusing the leaf package only for path/provenance decisions and the parent\n`settings` package for `EntireSettings` construction.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Write failing route-selection tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_GlobalFirstSelectsGitCommonAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ExplicitFirstSelectsWorktreeAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_CanceledWaiterDoesNotPoisonWinner(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_LinkedWorktreesAreIndependent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_ReadOnlyDoesNotCreateRegistry(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_CorruptRecordFailsClosed(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\n\nStore:\n\n```text\n<git-common-dir>/entire/worktree/<worktree-key>/route.json\n```\n\nUse:\n\n```go\ntype RuntimeRoute struct {\n\tVersion           int           `json:\"version\"`\n\tLayout            RuntimeLayout `json:\"layout\"`\n\tCanonicalWorktree string        `json:\"canonical_worktree\"`\n\tCanonicalGitCommon string       `json:\"canonical_git_common\"`\n}\n\nfunc ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, error)\nfunc EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) (RepoPolicy, error)\nfunc WithRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) context.Context\nfunc RepoPolicyFromContext(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, bool)\n```\n\nThe creation critical section covers only read/create/publish. Write and fsync\na complete `0600` temp file beneath a user-owned `0700` registry directory,\npublish without replacing an existing record, then reread the winner. On every\nread verify the full canonical worktree and Git-common identities before using\nthe short-hash namespace; a mismatch fails closed. Never hold this lock around\nhooks, prompts, Git operations, condensation, or runtime writes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\n\n`paths.AbsPath` should obtain a policy snapshot from context or call read-only classification as a compatibility fallback, then map only `metadata`, `logs`, and `tmp` through the selected route. Delete `repoActivationConfigured`, `userGlobalTierEnabled`, and duplicated JSON/settings parsing from `paths/invisible.go`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Run focused route/path tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|LoadForRepoPolicy|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS, including cancellation and separate-git-dir coverage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 11: Run duplication checks before commit**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: no new actionable duplication between `repopolicy` and `paths`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 12: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go cmd/entire/cli/paths\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): make activation and runtime routing sticky\"\n```\n\n---\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"### Task 2: Add machine-local activation provenance and sticky runtime routing\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settin