{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:00:00.440Z","ordinal":11114,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cdaff4bc087d0ba6e710491cc8864","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The rerun followed real compatibility failures, not flakiness. The implementation now distinguishes malformed repository content during read-only activation classification from malformed allowed fields at the hook-settings boundary: classification ignores repository content it must not trust, while hook-time sanitized loading still fails closed. Two legacy assertions were also updated for canonical paths and the intentional sticky-route contract."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787615999334,"completed_at_ms":1787616000440}}
